      ],
      "lineAnnotations": {
        "0": {"synopsis":"RST $00: where the IM 2 probe's interrupt arrives. The probe (NMI_TO_MENU) fills $5B00-$5C00\nwith $00 and sets I = $5B, so an IM 2 interrupt reads the vector $0000 and runs this: $3F2F\n= 2 (SET_INT_SEEN).\nChanges: nothing (AF kept; RET, not RETI)."},
        "1": {"comment":"2: the interrupt came through $0000"},
        "8": {"synopsis":"RST $08: an endless loop (a jump to itself). Nothing in this ROM executes RST $08.","comment":"Stays here for good"},
        "11": {"synopsis":"The text \".bin\", ended by $FF: the extension SAVE_BANKS adds to its file name ($07B9 passes\nDE = $000E, its last letter, to $1179, which compares it backwards)."},
        "16": {"synopsis":"RST $10: calls the routine in ROM 0 whose address is the word after the RST, then returns\npast the word. BC is kept at $5B54 for the call; $1558 reads the word and leaves through\nRAM_MF_OUT ($5C1C, the Multiface paged out), coming back through RAM_MF_IN ($5C23).\nExit: registers as the routine leaves them.","comment":"BC kept for the call"},
        "20": {"comment":"HL = the word's address; HL kept on the stack"},
        "21": {"comment":"On to the call"},
        "24": {"synopsis":"RST $18: as RST $10 for ROM 1 ($1576): NextReg $8E = 1 through RAM_ROM1 ($5B3E) for the\ncall, back to ROM 0 through RAM_ROM0 ($5B4D).","comment":"BC kept for the call"},
        "28": {"comment":"HL = the word's address; HL kept on the stack"},
        "29": {"comment":"On to the call"},
        "32": {"synopsis":"RST $20: as RST $10 for ROM 2 ($158F): NextReg $8E = 2 through RAM_ROM2 ($5B43), back to ROM\n0 through RAM_ROM0 ($5B4D).","comment":"BC kept for the call"},
        "36": {"comment":"HL = the word's address; HL kept on the stack"},
        "37": {"comment":"On to the call"},
        "40": {"synopsis":"RST $28: as RST $10 for ROM 3 ($15A8): NextReg $8E = 3 through RAM_ROM3 ($5B48), back to ROM\n0 through RAM_ROM0 ($5B4D).","comment":"BC kept for the call"},
        "44": {"comment":"HL = the word's address; HL kept on the stack"},
        "45": {"comment":"On to the call"},
        "48": {"synopsis":"RST $30: prints the character or window code A in the Multiface's current window: IX = the\nwindow at ($3F30) ($F700 normally, $FB00 for the 64-column screens), then ROM 0's\nWIN_PRINT_A_RAW ($2767) through RST $10 (PRINT_A_CALL).\nExit: BC and HL kept, IX = the window.","comment":"IX = the current window"},
        "52": {"comment":"BC and HL kept"},
        "56": {"synopsis":"RST $38, also the IM 1 interrupt while this ROM is paged in: $3F2F = 1 (SET_INT_SEEN),\ninterrupts on again, back. It ends the EI/HALT waits for a frame ($0268, $0463, $055B) and\nanswers the IM probe for IM 0/IM 1."},
        "57": {"comment":"1: the interrupt came through $0038"},
        "63": {"comment":"Interrupts back on"},
        "65": {"synopsis":"PRINT_A's print: ROM 0's WIN_PRINT_A_RAW ($2767) with the window at IX; HL and BC back.","comment":"Print A in the window (WIN_PRINT_A_RAW)"},
        "68": {"comment":"HL and BC back"},
        "71": {"synopsis":"Splits an address of the interrupted program's 64K map into its 8K page and offset: the MMU\nslot is H's bits 7-5, its page the copy of NextReg $50 + slot saved by the NMI at\n$3F6A-$3F71.\nEntry: HL = the address.\nExit: A = the 8K page, HL = the offset ($0000-$1FFF), DE = the address of the slot's copy,\nBC = the slot (0-7).","comment":"Slot = H's bits 7-5"},
        "77": {"comment":"BC = the slot"},
        "80": {"comment":"HL kept in DE"},
        "81": {"comment":"The saved MMU 0-7 pages"},
        "85": {"comment":"DE = this slot's copy; HL back"},
        "86": {"comment":"HL = the offset in the 8K page"},
        "90": {"comment":"A = the page"},
        "92": {"synopsis":"Moves a memory browser position on by one byte: in bank mode (C not $FF) the offset wraps\nwithin the 8K page, in address mode at 64K.\nEntry: HL = the offset or address, C = the 8K page or $FF.\nExit: HL = the next one; Z set when it wrapped round to 0.\nChanges: AF."},
        "93": {"comment":"Address mode (C = $FF)?"},
        "97": {"comment":"Bank mode: $2000 wraps to 0"},
        "99": {"synopsis":"The wrap test: Z when HL is 0.","comment":"Back to 0?"},
        "102": {"synopsis":"The NMI: on to NMI_ENTRY. The Multiface pages itself in at the fetch from $0066 (this ROM at\n$0000-$1FFF, its RAM at $2000-$3FFF; multiface.vhd); the NMI comes from the M1 button, a\nwrite of bit 3 to NextReg $02 (ROM 2's snapshot start, or a breakpoint) or a +3 FDC I/O trap\n(NextReg $D8)."},
        "105": {"synopsis":"$3F2F = A: which interrupt entry ran (1 at $0038, 2 at $0000), for the IM probe at $0264.","comment":"Interrupt entry seen"},
        "109": {"synopsis":"The NMI handler: saves the interrupted program's state and quietens the machine.\n1. SP is kept at $3FB1 and the registers pushed below $3FC4 into a block at $3FA9 laid out\n   like a .z80 header: AF $3FA9 (F first), BC $3FAB, HL $3FAD (and $3FAF, the PC slot), SP\n   $3FB1 (+2: as before the NMI), I $3FB3, R $3FB4 (less $13 for the handler's own fetches,\n   bit 7 kept), DE $3FB6, BC' $3FB8, DE' $3FBA, HL' $3FBC, AF' $3FBE, IY $3FC0, IX $3FC2,\n   IFF2 (the P/V flag of LD A,R) $3FC4. The stack is then $3916.\n2. The selected NextReg ($243B) is kept at $3F4B; the NextRegs listed at $0E76 go to\n   $3F4E-$3FA0 (SAVE_NEXTREGS: MMU 0-7 at $3F6A, the NMI return address $C2/$C3 at $3F9F),\n   then NextRegs $03 and $28, port $123B and port $E3 to $3FA1-$3FA4. Copper and expansion\n   bus are stopped.\n3. The Multiface's read-back ports give the last values written to $7FFD ($3FCC), $1FFD\n   ($3FFF), $DFFD ($3FA6) and $EFF7 ($3FA7), and the border (doubled, $3FB5); $DFFD and\n   $EFF7 are cleared.\n4. NextReg $02's NMI causes go to $3F2D (bit 0 NextReg $02, bit 1 an I/O trap) and are\n   cleared.\n5. The clip windows ($3F3A-$3F4A), the AY's selected register ($3FCF) and registers 0-15\n   ($3FD0-$3FDF) and the first ULA palette ($3E57, 32 entries of 2 bytes) are saved; the\n   AY's tone channels and volumes are switched off.\n6. On at MENU_SETUP.","comment":"SP of the program, less 2"},
        "113": {"comment":"Push the registers into $3FA9-$3FC3"},
        "116": {"comment":"IX to $3FC2, IY to $3FC0"},
        "120": {"comment":"AF' to $3FBE; AF kept in AF'"},
        "122": {"comment":"HL', DE', BC' to $3FBC-$3FB8"},
        "127": {"comment":"DE to $3FB6"},
        "128": {"comment":"A = R; P/V = IFF2"},
        "131": {"comment":"E = those flags"},
        "132": {"comment":"D = the flags too"},
        "133": {"comment":"Flags to $3FB4 and $3FB5"},
        "134": {"comment":"Then R to $3FB4 and I to $3FB3"},
        "140": {"comment":"Past the SP slot at $3FB1"},
        "142": {"comment":"HL to $3FAF (the PC slot) and $3FAD"},
        "144": {"comment":"BC to $3FAB"},
        "145": {"comment":"AF to $3FA9"},
        "147": {"comment":"The Multiface's own stack"},
        "150": {"comment":"$3FB1 = SP as before the NMI"},
        "158": {"comment":"IFF2 (flag bit 2) to $3FC4"},
        "168": {"comment":"R less $13; bit 7 kept"},
        "184": {"comment":"The NextReg selected now"},
        "189": {"comment":"Kept at $3F4B"},
        "192": {"comment":"The NextRegs listed at $0E76 to $3F4E"},
        "195": {"comment":"Copper stopped"},
        "199": {"comment":"Expansion bus off"},
        "202": {"comment":"NextReg $03 (machine type) to $3FA1"},
        "209": {"comment":"NextReg $28 (palette byte held) to $3FA2"},
        "216": {"comment":"Layer 2 port to $3FA3"},
        "223": {"comment":"DivMMC control to $3FA4"},
        "226": {"comment":"Last $7FFD value (Multiface read-back)"},
        "231": {"comment":"Kept at $3FCC"},
        "234": {"comment":"Last $1FFD value"},
        "239": {"comment":"Kept at $3FFF"},
        "242": {"comment":"Last $DFFD value"},
        "247": {"comment":"Kept at $3FA6"},
        "250": {"comment":"$DFFD = 0"},
        "255": {"comment":"Last $EFF7 value (bits 2-3)"},
        "260": {"comment":"Kept at $3FA7"},
        "263": {"comment":"$EFF7 = 0"},
        "268": {"comment":"The border colour"},
        "275": {"comment":"Doubled: bits 1-3 of $3FB5"},
        "279": {"comment":"NextReg $02: the NMI's cause"},
        "284": {"comment":"Kept in D"},
        "285": {"comment":"Bit 7 kept, the NMI causes cleared"},
        "289": {"comment":"Bits 4-3 (trap, NextReg) to bits 1-0"},
        "298": {"comment":"Clip windows to $3F3A-$3F4A"},
        "301": {"comment":"NextReg $1C: the clip indices","synopsis":"NextReg $1C read for the clip indices, within NMI_ENTRY. The CALL $012D at $13xx is not a call of here: that\ncode runs at $5B00 with ROM 2 selected, where $012D is ROM 2's DOS_SET_DRIVE."},
        "308": {"comment":"All four clip indices reset"},
        "312": {"comment":"NextRegs $18-$1B, four bytes each"},
        "316": {"synopsis":"One clip window register."},
        "318": {"synopsis":"One coordinate."},
        "319": {"comment":"Read one coordinate"},
        "325": {"comment":"Written back: the index moves on"},
        "330": {"comment":"Next register"},
        "334": {"comment":"The AY register selected now"},
        "339": {"comment":"Kept at $3FCF"},
        "344": {"comment":"AY registers 0-15 to $3FD0"},
        "349": {"synopsis":"One AY register."},
        "352": {"comment":"Select register D"},
        "354": {"comment":"Read it"},
        "358": {"comment":"All 16?"},
        "363": {"comment":"Register 7 (mixer) = $FF: all off"},
        "372": {"synopsis":"One volume register.","comment":"Registers 8, 9 and 10 = 0"},
        "380": {"comment":"Up to register 10?"},
        "384": {"comment":"First ULA palette (32 entries) to $3E57"},
        "389": {"comment":"NextReg $43 = 0"},
        "393": {"synopsis":"Sets the machine for the menu, after NMI_ENTRY, or again from BACK_TO_MENU with the\nprogram's state still saved:\n1. Layer 2 port and DivMMC off, NextReg $8F = 0 (standard paging); the NextRegs at\n   NR_INIT_REGS ($17CC) get NR_INIT_VALUES ($17F2) (WRITE_NEXTREGS), MMU 0-7 among them =\n   $FF $FF $0A $0B $04 $05 $00 $01.\n2. NextReg $06 bits 4-3 cleared (no NMI by the DRIVE or M1 button), NextReg $05 = (it AND 5)\n   OR $5A, NextReg $08 = (it AND $FD) OR $C4 ($7FFD unlocked, no contention, port $FF\n   readable, TurboSound off).\n3. Port $FF kept at $3FA5 and cleared.\n4. By $3F2D: bit 7 ($FE/$FF, back from SET_EXIT_MODE): NMI_MENU_SETUP. Exactly 1 (NMI by\n   NextReg $02 only) with the NMI return address $0AB8 or $0AB9 (ROM 2's SNAP_START),\n   NextReg $8C's copy not 10 in bits 7-6, ROM 2 paged and MMU 0-1 = $FF: step 5. Anything\n   else: NMI_TO_MENU.\n5. ROM 2 has loaded a snapshot: MMU 0-5's copies = $FF $FF $0A $0B $04 $05 ($17FD), MMU\n   6-7's = 2 x the bank in $5D46 bits 0-2, +1; NextReg $08's copy bit 7 = not $5D46 bit 5;\n   NextReg $82's and $8C's copies = E and D (the DE of ROM 2's code); the 87-byte header at\n   $5D23 over $3FA9; the NMI return address = its PC ($3FC9); its A/F pairs swapped when\n   $3FB5 bit 0 is set (SWAP_AF_BYTES); RAM image installed, stack at $5E00; RESTORE_MEMORY\n   with carry.","comment":"Layer 2 port = 0"},
        "399": {"comment":"DivMMC paged out"},
        "401": {"comment":"Standard ZX 128K +3 paging"},
        "405": {"comment":"The menu's values for the NextReg list"},
        "414": {"comment":"NextReg $06"},
        "421": {"comment":"No NMI by DRIVE (bit 4) or M1 (bit 3)"},
        "426": {"comment":"NextReg $05"},
        "433": {"comment":"50/60 Hz and scandoubler kept","synopsis":"The peripheral setting's 50/60 Hz and scandoubler bits kept, the joystick bits set. The CALL $01B1 in the\ncode run at $5B00 with ROM 2 selected is ROM 2's IDE_PATH, not a call of here."},
        "435": {"comment":"Joystick mode bits 6, 4, 3 and 1 set"},
        "440": {"comment":"NextReg $08"},
        "447": {"comment":"TurboSound off"},
        "449": {"comment":"$7FFD unlocked, no contention, port $FF on"},
        "453": {"comment":"Timex port $FF to $3FA5"},
        "458": {"comment":"Standard screen mode"},
        "461": {"comment":"The NMI's cause"},
        "464": {"comment":"$FE/$FF (back from SET_EXIT_MODE)?"},
        "468": {"comment":"Button NMI?"},
        "470": {"comment":"Only the NextReg $02 bit?"},
        "473": {"comment":"The NMI return address (NextRegs $C2/$C3)"},
        "476": {"comment":"$0AB8?"},
        "483": {"comment":"$0AB9?"},
        "488": {"synopsis":"The NMI came from ROM 2's snapshot start: are the alternate ROM, the ROM and MMU 0-1 as it\nleaves them?","comment":"NextReg $8C's copy"},
        "491": {"comment":"Bits 7-6 = 10?"},
        "497": {"comment":"A = the ROM paged x 2"},
        "500": {"comment":"ROM 2?"},
        "504": {"comment":"MMU 0 and 1's copies"},
        "509": {"comment":"Both $FF (ROM)?"},
        "513": {"comment":"DE = MMU 0's copy"},
        "514": {"comment":"MMU 0-5 = $FF $FF $0A $0B $04 $05"},
        "522": {"comment":"The bank in $5D46 bits 0-2"},
        "528": {"comment":"MMU 6 = bank x 2"},
        "531": {"comment":"MMU 7 = bank x 2 + 1"},
        "533": {"comment":"$5D46 bit 5 set?"},
        "535": {"comment":"NextReg $08's copy: bit 7 set"},
        "542": {"comment":"Cleared for bit 5 set"},
        "544": {"synopsis":"The NextReg copies from DE, the header, then the restore.","comment":"DE of the code that raised the NMI"},
        "547": {"comment":"E to NextReg $82's copy"},
        "551": {"comment":"D to NextReg $8C's copy"},
        "555": {"comment":"The 87-byte header at $5D23 to $3FA9"},
        "566": {"comment":"Its PC as the NMI return address"},
        "572": {"comment":"Bit 0 of $3FB5 set?"},
        "575": {"comment":"Then the A/F pairs swapped"},
        "579": {"comment":"RAM image at $5B00"},
        "582": {"comment":"A stack in RAM"},
        "585": {"comment":"Carry: the snapshot start"},
        "589": {"synopsis":"An NMI for the menu:\n1. $5B00-$5DFF kept at $3B54 in the Multiface's RAM.\n2. The IM probe: $5B00-$5C00 = $00, I = $5B, one interrupt waited for; $3F2F (1 through\n   INT_IM1, 2 through INT_IM2) goes to $3FC6, the header's IM byte.\n3. IM 1, IY = $5C3A; on at NMI_MENU_SETUP.","comment":"$5B00-$5DFF to $3B54"},
        "601": {"comment":"$5B00 = $00"},
        "603": {"comment":"And on to $5C00"},
        "606": {"comment":"BC = $0100"},
        "607": {"comment":"I = $5B: IM 2 vector $0000"},
        "610": {"comment":"$5B00-$5C00 = $00"},
        "612": {"comment":"No interrupt seen yet"},
        "616": {"comment":"Wait for one"},
        "618": {"comment":"1 or 2: the interrupt mode"},
        "621": {"comment":"To $3FC6 (the header's IM byte)"},
        "624": {"comment":"IM 1 for the menu"},
        "626": {"comment":"The system variables' base"},
        "630": {"synopsis":"The menu's set-up:\n1. $3E97 = 0 (no overlay at $F720), 28MHz, RAM image at $5B00 (INSTALL_RAM), stack at $5E00.\n2. RAM_SNAP_START ($5B8A): no carry (not NextZXOS 2.08): straight back to the program\n   (NMI_RESTORE). Carry: the program's memory the Multiface uses is now in DivMMC banks.\n3. ROM 0's state bytes $D5B9-$D5BD = INIT_D5B9; the saved $5B00-$5DFF copied on to DivMMC\n   bank 6's $3B00 (through $5E00); $6000-$77FF kept at $2000 in the Multiface's RAM.\n4. The page cache emptied (CACHE_RESET), $D5BB = the CPU speed (NextReg $07's copy, bits\n   1-0), ROM 0's $100C (in COLSET1_APPLY) and COPY_STRIPES, the breakpoints taken out\n   (BP_REMOVE_ALL).\n5. The first drive (0-15) whose entry at $387F + 22 x drive in DivMMC memory (ROM 2's\n   MMC13_PEEK) has bit 3 set and whose flags byte (ROM 2's DRIVE_FLAGS) is $4D goes to $3A53\n   with bit 7 set ($10 if none); its flags byte becomes $80 meanwhile (DRIVE_FLAG_SET). When\n   it was the default drive ($3A52), C becomes the default.\n6. On at MENU_NMI_CAUSE.","comment":"No overlay loaded at $F720"},
        "634": {"comment":"28MHz"},
        "638": {"comment":"RAM image at $5B00"},
        "641": {"comment":"Stack below $5E00"},
        "644": {"comment":"Version check; memory to DivMMC banks"},
        "647": {"comment":"No carry: back to the program"},
        "650": {"comment":"ROM 0's state $D5B9-$D5BD"},
        "661": {"comment":"The saved $5B00-$5DFF to bank 6's $3B00"},
        "669": {"synopsis":"One 256-byte block."},
        "671": {"comment":"Through $5E00"},
        "679": {"comment":"DE back; the source kept"},
        "681": {"comment":"Then into DivMMC bank 6"},
        "689": {"comment":"Bank 6 via RAM_DIVMMC_LDIR"},
        "696": {"comment":"$6000-$77FF to $2000 (Multiface RAM)"},
        "707": {"comment":"Page cache emptied"},
        "710": {"comment":"CPU speed bits of NextReg $07's copy"},
        "715": {"comment":"Into ROM 0's state"},
        "718": {"comment":"ROM 0's $100C (in COLSET1_APPLY)"},
        "721": {"comment":"ROM 0's COPY_STRIPES"},
        "724": {"comment":"Breakpoints taken out"},
        "727": {"comment":"16 drives; C = the drive"},
        "730": {"comment":"Their entries in DivMMC memory, 22 bytes each"},
        "733": {"synopsis":"One drive."},
        "735": {"comment":"A = the entry's byte (MMC13_PEEK)"},
        "740": {"comment":"Bit 3 set?"},
        "745": {"comment":"A = the drive"},
        "746": {"comment":"Its flags byte, doubled (DRIVE_FLAGS)"},
        "750": {"comment":"Flags byte halved"},
        "751": {"comment":"$4D?"},
        "755": {"comment":"Found: bit 7 marks it"},
        "759": {"synopsis":"The next drive.","comment":"Next entry"},
        "766": {"synopsis":"Found, or none ($10).","comment":"Drive found, or $10"},
        "770": {"comment":"Its flags byte = $80 meanwhile"},
        "777": {"comment":"$80 + drive becomes the drive's letter"},
        "782": {"comment":"The default drive?"},
        "785": {"comment":"Then C becomes the default"},
        "787": {"comment":"DOS_SET_DRIVE"},
        "790": {"synopsis":"Acts on the NMI's cause ($3F2D, then cleared): bit 0 (NextReg $02: a breakpoint; also $FF\nafter VIEW_SCREEN) runs the breakpoint handler at $0BC6; 2-15 (bit 1, an I/O trap) runs\nIO_TRAP; $FE runs neither. Then the main menu.","comment":"The cause, cleared"},
        "796": {"comment":"Bit 0: NMI by NextReg $02?"},
        "799": {"comment":"Then the breakpoint handler"},
        "803": {"comment":"$FE/$FF?"},
        "807": {"comment":"2-15: an I/O trap"},
        "812": {"synopsis":"The NMI menu: the screen cleared (ROM 3's CLS_CMD), then MAIN_MENU_SHOW.","comment":"Clear the screen (CLS_CMD)"},
        "815": {"synopsis":"Shows the main menu (\"NMI Menu\": Snapshot, Screenshot, TAP Files, POKEs, Debug Tools,\nSettings, Keymap, About; $13E6) in the window at $F700. BREAK (carry): MENU_EXIT. A choice:\nMENU_DISPATCH, then MAIN_MENU.","comment":"The window at $F700"},
        "818": {"comment":"Window code $18, then ATTR_P"},
        "825": {"comment":"Run the menu: A = the choice"},
        "828": {"comment":"Kept over the CLS"},
        "829": {"comment":"Clear the screen (CLS_CMD)"},
        "833": {"comment":"BREAK: back to the program"},
        "836": {"comment":"Run the choice"},
        "841": {"synopsis":"A +3 FDC I/O trap (NextReg $D8 bit 0): FDC_TRAP_MSG shown (\"ERROR ... This program has\nattempted to access the +3 FDC hardware ...\"), a click, then the keys: D runs the breakpoint\nhandler ($0BC6), I clears NextReg $D8's copy (no more traps) and returns to the program\n(MENU_EXIT); reset is the third way out.","comment":"Clear the screen (CLS_CMD)"},
        "844": {"comment":"The FDC message"},
        "850": {"comment":"A click (CLICK)"},
        "853": {"synopsis":"Waits while I is held.","comment":"Keyboard row Y-P"},
        "857": {"comment":"I (bit 2) still held?"},
        "861": {"synopsis":"One key.","comment":"A = the key (WAIT_KEY_CLICK)"},
        "864": {"comment":"Upper case"},
        "866": {"comment":"D: the debugger"},
        "871": {"comment":"I?"},
        "875": {"comment":"NextReg $D8's copy = 0: no traps"},
        "878": {"comment":"Back to the program"},
        "881": {"synopsis":"Copies the RAM image ($1856-$1AAF, $025A bytes) to $5B00-$5D59.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL.","comment":"The RAM image"},
        "887": {"synopsis":"Copies BC bytes from HL to $5B00 (RESTORE_MEMORY puts code there to run).\nChanges: BC, DE, HL."},
        "893": {"synopsis":"Runs main menu choice A: 0 Snapshot (SNAPSHOT), 4 Debug Tools (DEBUG_MENU); the others load\noverlay D (MENU_OVERLAY): 1 Screenshot 2, 2 TAP Files 3, 3 POKEs 4, 5 Settings 5, 6 Keymap\n6, 7 About 1.","comment":"0: Snapshot"},
        "897": {"comment":"1: Screenshot, overlay 2"},
        "902": {"comment":"2: TAP Files, overlay 3"},
        "907": {"comment":"3: POKEs, overlay 4"},
        "912": {"comment":"4: Debug Tools"},
        "916": {"comment":"5: Settings, overlay 5"},
        "921": {"comment":"6: Keymap, overlay 6"},
        "926": {"comment":"7: About, overlay 1"},
        "928": {"synopsis":"Loads overlay D, c:/nextzxos/enMfD.sys, at $F720 unless it is there already ($12AD), and\njumps to its code at $F722. When it cannot be loaded, MAIN_MENU_SHOW without clearing the\nscreen.","comment":"Overlay D at $F720"},
        "931": {"comment":"Loaded: run it"},
        "934": {"comment":"Return address dropped"},
        "937": {"synopsis":"Key V on the status screen (key table at $1477): shows the program's screen until SPACE.\n$3F2D = $FF, so that NMI_RESTORE goes to VIEW_WAIT_PRESS; SET_EXIT_MODE.","comment":"After the restore: VIEW_WAIT_PRESS"},
        "939": {"synopsis":"$3F2D = A ($FF or $FE: what NMI_RESTORE does once the machine is set back), NextReg $06's\ncopy without its NMI button bits 4-3; MENU_EXIT.","comment":"What to do once restored"},
        "942": {"comment":"NextReg $06's copy"},
        "946": {"comment":"No NMI by the buttons meanwhile"},
        "949": {"comment":"Restore and leave"},
        "951": {"synopsis":"The program's screen is up (NMI_RESTORE with $3F2D = $FF; its registers not yet back): waits\nfor SPACE to be pressed, then released, then BACK_TO_MENU.","comment":"Keyboard row B-SPACE"},
        "956": {"comment":"SPACE not down yet?"},
        "960": {"synopsis":"Waits for SPACE to be released."},
        "965": {"comment":"SPACE still down?"},
        "969": {"synopsis":"NextReg $06's copy gets bit 3 (the M1 button's NMI) back; the menu entered again at\nMENU_SETUP, the program's state still saved.","comment":"M1 button NMI back in the copy"},
        "976": {"comment":"The menu again"},
        "979": {"synopsis":"$3F2D = $FE, then SET_EXIT_MODE: once the program's paging and NextRegs are back,\nDRVAPI_CALL runs. Nothing in this ROM refers to it.","comment":"After the restore: DRVAPI_CALL"},
        "983": {"synopsis":"With the program's paging and NextRegs set back ($3F2D = $FE): RAM image at $5B00, stack at\n$5E00, then the esxDOS call M_DRVAPI ($92) with C = $50 (the driver id) and B = $F6 (the\ncall id) through API_CALL ($1569, RST $08 at $5B5D); then BACK_TO_MENU.","comment":"RAM image at $5B00"},
        "994": {"comment":"A stack in RAM"},
        "997": {"comment":"Driver $50, call $F6"},
        "1000": {"comment":"M_DRVAPI through RST $08"},
        "1006": {"synopsis":"Key C on the status and breakpoint screens (key tables at $1477 and $14D7): the breakpoints\nplanted (BP_PLANT_ALL), then MENU_EXIT.","comment":"Breakpoints planted"},
        "1009": {"synopsis":"Leaves the menu for the program:\n1. The page cache written back (CACHE_FLUSH); $6000-$77FF back from $2000.\n2. NextReg $07's copy = ROM 0's CPU speed byte $D5BB.\n3. The drive found at the menu's entry ($3A53) gets its flags byte $4D back\n   (DRIVE_FLAG_SET).\n4. RESTORE_MEMORY without carry.","comment":"Page cache written back"},
        "1012": {"comment":"$6000-$77FF back"},
        "1023": {"comment":"CPU speed from ROM 0's state"},
        "1030": {"comment":"The drive found at entry"},
        "1033": {"comment":"Its flags byte back to $4D"},
        "1038": {"comment":"No carry: from the menu"},
        "1039": {"synopsis":"Puts the program's memory back.\nEntry: carry for ROM 2's snapshot start (MENU_SETUP), none from the menu.\n1. Bank 6's $3B00-$3DFF (the program's $5B00-$5DFF) back to $3B54, through $5E00.\n2. Interrupts off. With carry, only the code at $13A5 runs, copied to $5B00: $4000-$5AFF and\n   $5E00-$5FFF from DivMMC bank 6, $C000-$FFFF from banks 4 and 5. Without, ROM 2\n   (RAM_ROM2), then $135A run at $5B00 (default drive and path back, $A000-$BFFF from bank\n   11), then $138B ($3916-$3A51 kept in bank 12, then as $13A5).\n3. On at NMI_RESTORE.","comment":"Carry kept"},
        "1040": {"comment":"Bank 6's $3B00-$3DFF back to $3B54"},
        "1048": {"synopsis":"One 256-byte block."},
        "1050": {"comment":"Through $5E00"},
        "1056": {"comment":"From DivMMC bank 6"},
        "1063": {"comment":"Then to the Multiface's RAM"},
        "1075": {"comment":"No interrupts now"},
        "1076": {"comment":"Snapshot start?"},
        "1077": {"comment":"Only the memory restore"},
        "1082": {"comment":"ROM 2 for the DOS calls"},
        "1085": {"comment":"Drive, path and $A000-$BFFF back"},
        "1094": {"comment":"Run at $5B00"},
        "1097": {"comment":"Menu state kept, then the memory restore"},
        "1100": {"synopsis":"Copies $5B bytes from HL to $5B00 and runs them."},
        "1106": {"comment":"Run at $5B00"},
        "1109": {"synopsis":"Returns to the interrupted program:\n1. Stack at $3916; $5B00-$5DFF back from $3B54; one interrupt waited for.\n2. The first ULA palette from $3E57 (WRITE_PALETTE), the clip windows with each index moved\n   back where it was, the border, NextReg $8F, ports $DFFD, $EFF7, $1FFD, $7FFD and $FF.\n3. The saved NextRegs written back (RESTORE_NEXTREGS) with NextReg $07 cut to its speed bits\n   and a Copper mode 01 (start from index 0) made 10 (carry on); then the palette byte\n   NextReg $44 held (NextReg $03 bit 7), port $123B without bits 0 and 2, the NextReg\n   selected.\n4. $3F2D = $FF: VIEW_WAIT_PRESS; $FE: DRVAPI_CALL.\n5. The AY's registers and selection; OUT to port $3F (the Multiface's NMI state ends); ports\n   $123B and $E3; R less $11; $3FB1 back to SP as the NMI left it.\n6. One interrupt waited for; IM and IFF1 set; the registers popped from $3FA9; RETN, which\n   pages the Multiface out (and takes the return address from NextRegs $C2/$C3 when NextReg\n   $C0's stackless NMI is on).","comment":"The Multiface's own stack"},
        "1112": {"comment":"$5B00-$5DFF back"},
        "1123": {"comment":"Wait for an interrupt"},
        "1126": {"comment":"First ULA palette back from $3E57"},
        "1131": {"comment":"NextReg $43 = 0"},
        "1132": {"comment":"Two bytes an entry"},
        "1136": {"comment":"Clip windows: the indices"},
        "1141": {"comment":"All indices reset"},
        "1145": {"comment":"NextRegs $18-$1B"},
        "1149": {"synopsis":"One clip window."},
        "1152": {"comment":"Its four coordinates"},
        "1158": {"comment":"HL = them again; the next window's kept"},
        "1160": {"comment":"This window's saved index"},
        "1163": {"comment":"Write that many again: the index back"},
        "1167": {"comment":"Next index into bits 1-0"},
        "1174": {"comment":"Border colour back"},
        "1181": {"comment":"Paging mode back"},
        "1187": {"comment":"$DFFD back"},
        "1195": {"comment":"$EFF7 back"},
        "1203": {"comment":"$1FFD back"},
        "1211": {"comment":"$7FFD back"},
        "1219": {"comment":"Timex port $FF back"},
        "1224": {"comment":"Copper control's copy, kept"},
        "1229": {"comment":"Bits 7-6 = 00 (stopped)?"},
        "1235": {"comment":"11?"},
        "1241": {"comment":"01 or 10: 10, carry on where it was"},
        "1245": {"synopsis":"The Copper control byte to write."},
        "1248": {"comment":"NextReg $07's copy, kept"},
        "1253": {"comment":"Only the speed bits written"},
        "1256": {"comment":"The saved NextRegs back"},
        "1259": {"comment":"Copies put back as saved"},
        "1267": {"comment":"NextReg $03 bit 7: a palette byte held?"},
        "1270": {"comment":"NextReg $28's copy: the byte"},
        "1272": {"comment":"None held?"},
        "1274": {"comment":"Held byte back into NextReg $44"},
        "1277": {"synopsis":"Port $123B without its paging bits 0 and 2.","comment":"Layer 2 port without bits 0 and 2"},
        "1285": {"comment":"The NextReg selected at the NMI"},
        "1293": {"comment":"What to do now?"},
        "1297": {"comment":"$FF: VIEW_WAIT_PRESS"},
        "1300": {"comment":"$FE: DRVAPI_CALL"},
        "1303": {"comment":"AY registers 0-15 back"},
        "1308": {"synopsis":"One AY register."},
        "1311": {"comment":"Select register D"},
        "1315": {"comment":"Write its value"},
        "1320": {"comment":"All 16?"},
        "1324": {"comment":"The AY register selected at the NMI"},
        "1332": {"comment":"The Multiface's NMI state ends"},
        "1334": {"comment":"Layer 2 port back"},
        "1342": {"comment":"DivMMC control back"},
        "1347": {"comment":"R less $11; bit 7 kept"},
        "1363": {"comment":"SP slot back to the return address"},
        "1371": {"comment":"Wait for an interrupt"},
        "1374": {"comment":"IM 0, 1 or 2 from $3FC6"},
        "1390": {"synopsis":"IFF1 back.","comment":"IFF1 at the NMI"},
        "1396": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "1397": {"synopsis":"The registers back from the block at $3FA9, then RETN.","comment":"Pop the registers from $3FA9"},
        "1400": {"comment":"AF kept in AF'"},
        "1402": {"comment":"BC, then HL"},
        "1404": {"comment":"The PC slot skipped"},
        "1405": {"comment":"I from $3FB3"},
        "1409": {"comment":"R from $3FB4"},
        "1413": {"comment":"DE from $3FB6"},
        "1415": {"comment":"BC', DE', HL'"},
        "1420": {"comment":"AF' and AF back"},
        "1422": {"comment":"IY, IX"},
        "1426": {"comment":"SP of the program"},
        "1430": {"comment":"Back; the Multiface pages out"},
        "1432": {"synopsis":"Writes a drive's flags byte: when A = $80 + drive, B goes to $2310 + drive in DivMMC memory\n(selector 0) through ROM 2's MMC0_POKE.\nEntry: A = $80 + the drive, or below $80 for none; B = the byte.\nExit: carry and nothing done for A below $80.","comment":"No drive marked?"},
        "1435": {"comment":"Its flags byte at $2310 + drive"},
        "1440": {"comment":"The value"},
        "1441": {"comment":"Written (MMC0_POKE)"},
        "1445": {"synopsis":"Writes E bytes from HL to NextReg D, one after another (a clip window's coordinates).\nExit: HL past them, E = 0.\nChanges: AF, BC.","comment":"Select NextReg D"},
        "1451": {"comment":"The next byte"},
        "1455": {"comment":"E bytes?"},
        "1459": {"synopsis":"Is the program locked into 48K? Z when the $7FFD copy has bit 5 set (paging locked) or\nNextReg $8C's copy has $A in bits 7-4.\nExit: carry clear.","comment":"$7FFD's copy"},
        "1462": {"comment":"Paging locked?"},
        "1467": {"comment":"NextReg $8C's copy"},
        "1472": {"comment":"Bits 7-4 = $A?"},
        "1474": {"comment":"Carry clear"},
        "1477": {"synopsis":"Classifies the ROM the program runs with, for the snapshot: reads the word at $0066 and the\nbyte at $09A2 of the ROM it sees ($15C1), with NextReg $8C's copy set to $A0 and MMU 0's to\n$FF meanwhile.\nExit: carry and B = 0 (word $CBFD), 1 ($3C08) or 2 (another); or no carry and B = 3 (word\n$E5F5 and CHECK_48K's Z), 4 (word $E5F5, byte $53) or 5 (word $E5F5, another byte). C = the\nbyte at $09A2.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"NextReg $8C's copy kept in E"},
        "1481": {"comment":"$A0 meanwhile"},
        "1483": {"comment":"MMU 0's copy kept in D"},
        "1487": {"comment":"$FF (ROM) meanwhile"},
        "1490": {"comment":"The word at the ROM's $0066"},
        "1497": {"comment":"The byte at $09A2"},
        "1503": {"comment":"Kept in C"},
        "1506": {"comment":"The copies back"},
        "1514": {"comment":"$F5 $E5 (PUSH AF, PUSH HL) at $0066?"},
        "1522": {"comment":"B = 0"},
        "1524": {"comment":"$FD $CB?"},
        "1530": {"comment":"Carry, B = 0: yes"},
        "1532": {"comment":"B = 1"},
        "1533": {"comment":"$08 $3C?"},
        "1541": {"comment":"B = 2, carry: another ROM"},
        "1543": {"synopsis":"PUSH AF, PUSH HL at $0066: B = 3 when CHECK_48K says 48K, 4 when the byte at $09A2 is $53,\nelse 5; no carry.","comment":"Locked into 48K?"},
        "1546": {"comment":"B = 3"},
        "1549": {"comment":"B = 4"},
        "1550": {"comment":"$53 at $09A2?"},
        "1554": {"comment":"B = 5"},
        "1555": {"comment":"No carry"},
        "1557": {"synopsis":"The last 31 bytes of the snapshot header (its bytes 55-85), copied to $3FE0 by\nZ80_HEADER_BUILD: $03 $00 $00 $00 $00 $00 $FF $FF, then $03 $01 $03 $02 $03 $04 $03 $08 $03\n$10, then '1' $00 '2' $00 '3' $00 '4' $00 '5' $00, then $00 $00 $00."},
        "1588": {"synopsis":"Completes the snapshot header at $3FA9 for saving:\n1. $3FB5 (border x 2) gets R's bit 7 in bit 0.\n2. $3FC6: the IM (3 made 2), bit 2 = NextReg $08 bit 0 (issue 2 keyboard).\n3. $3FC7 = 55 (the extra header's length), $3FAF (the PC slot) = 0, $3FC9 = the PC (NextRegs\n   $C2/$C3), $3FCD = 0, $3FCE = 3 + 4 x NextReg $84's copy bit 0 (AY ports decoded), $3FC5\n   (IFF2) = IFF1.\n4. $3FE0-$3FFE from Z80_HDR_TAIL.\n5. $3FCB, the hardware byte, from IDENTIFY_ROM's B: 0 $50, 1 $51, 3 0, 4 4, others $0C.\n6. The A/F pairs swapped, A first (SWAP_AF_BYTES).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Bit 0 of $3FB5 = R's bit 7"},
        "1593": {"comment":"R"},
        "1596": {"comment":"Its bit 7 into carry"},
        "1599": {"comment":"NextReg $08: bit 0 (issue 2 keyboard)"},
        "1606": {"comment":"To bit 2"},
        "1609": {"comment":"The IM byte"},
        "1615": {"comment":"3?"},
        "1619": {"comment":"Then 2"},
        "1621": {"synopsis":"The IM byte with the keyboard bit.","comment":"IM with bit 2"},
        "1623": {"comment":"Extra header length 55"},
        "1629": {"comment":"PC slot 0"},
        "1634": {"comment":"PC from NextRegs $C2/$C3"},
        "1640": {"comment":"$3FCD = 0"},
        "1644": {"comment":"NextReg $84's copy: bit 0 (AY ports)"},
        "1649": {"comment":"To bit 2, with bits 1-0 set"},
        "1656": {"comment":"IFF2 = IFF1"},
        "1662": {"comment":"Bytes 55-85 of the header"},
        "1673": {"comment":"B = the ROM's class"},
        "1676": {"comment":"B = 1: $51"},
        "1681": {"comment":"B = 0: $50"},
        "1685": {"comment":"B = 4: 4"},
        "1690": {"comment":"B = 3: 0"},
        "1694": {"comment":"Others $0C"},
        "1696": {"synopsis":"The hardware byte to $3FCB, then the A/F pairs swapped.","comment":"The hardware byte"},
        "1701": {"synopsis":"Undoes what Z80_HEADER_BUILD changed that the restore uses: the IM byte cut to bits 1-0, the\nA/F pairs swapped back (SWAP_AF_BYTES).","comment":"IM byte without the keyboard bit"},
        "1708": {"synopsis":"Exchanges the two bytes of AF at $3FA9 and of AF' at $3FBE.\nChanges: DE, HL.","comment":"AF's two bytes"},
        "1717": {"comment":"The two bytes of AF'"},
        "1727": {"synopsis":"Main menu 0, Snapshot: refuses (TXT_CLASSIC_ONLY, \"Can only snapshot classic software (not\nNext or +3)\", a click, a key) when IDENTIFY_ROM gives carry with B 2 or more; otherwise\nSNAPSHOT_SAVE.","comment":"Classify the ROM"},
        "1730": {"comment":"Known ROM: save"},
        "1732": {"comment":"B = 0 or 1?"},
        "1737": {"comment":"The refusal"},
        "1743": {"comment":"A click (CLICK)"},
        "1746": {"comment":"Wait for a key (WAIT_KEY_CLICK)"},
        "1750": {"synopsis":"Saves the program as a .z80 file:\n1. The header completed (Z80_HEADER_BUILD).\n2. The file browser ($110F, types FILETYPES_Z80, help HELP_SAVE_Z80); nothing chosen:\n   SNAP_DONE.\n3. The name asked for (\"Save snapshot as:\", $1163); \"Saving...\" shown.\n4. \".z80\" added when missing ($1179), the file opened ($1227, ROM 2's DOS_OPEN), the 87-byte\n   header written ($1253).\n5. Hardware byte 0 (48K): banks 2, the one at $C000 (MMU 6's copy / 2) and 5 as pages 4, 5\n   and 8 ($1268); otherwise SAVE_128K.\n6. SNAP_CLOSE, SNAP_DONE. A DOS error is shown by ROM 0's SHOW_DOS_ERROR (SNAP_ERR); no\n   name: error $14.\nExit: carry clear on an error.","comment":"Complete the header"},
        "1753": {"comment":"Choose a .Z80 file"},
        "1762": {"comment":"Nothing chosen?"},
        "1764": {"comment":"Ask for the name"},
        "1774": {"comment":"\"Saving...\""},
        "1782": {"comment":"No name?"},
        "1785": {"comment":"\".z80\" added when missing"},
        "1791": {"comment":"Open the file"},
        "1794": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "1797": {"comment":"The 87-byte header"},
        "1806": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "1808": {"comment":"The hardware byte: 48K?"},
        "1814": {"comment":"Bank 2 as page 4"},
        "1822": {"comment":"Page 5: the bank at $C000"},
        "1824": {"comment":"MMU 6's copy"},
        "1827": {"comment":"Halved: its bank"},
        "1835": {"comment":"Bank 5 as page 8"},
        "1843": {"comment":"Close"},
        "1845": {"synopsis":"Banks 0-7 as pages 3-10.","comment":"Page 3 = bank 0"},
        "1848": {"synopsis":"One bank."},
        "1855": {"comment":"Next page and bank"},
        "1857": {"comment":"All eight?"},
        "1861": {"synopsis":"The file closed ($124B, ROM 2's DOS_CLOSE).","comment":"Close the file"},
        "1864": {"synopsis":"The header's changes undone (Z80_HEADER_UNDO), flags kept."},
        "1865": {"comment":"Header as the restore wants it"},
        "1870": {"synopsis":"No name: error $14.","comment":"Error $14"},
        "1872": {"synopsis":"Shows DOS error A (ROM 0's SHOW_DOS_ERROR), then SNAP_CLOSE.","comment":"Show the error (SHOW_DOS_ERROR)"},
        "1877": {"synopsis":"SPACE in a debugger screen ($1441): the window back to normal ($10C1), then DEBUG_MENU.","comment":"Back to the normal window"},
        "1880": {"synopsis":"Main menu 4, Debug Tools: the menu text at $10D5 (\"Debug\": Status, Memory Browser,\nBreakpoints, Save 8K Banks) run by $13EC. BREAK: back to the main menu. 0: the status screen\n($0BFB); 1: MEM_BROWSER; 2: the breakpoints ($0ED6); 3: SAVE_BANKS.","comment":"Clear the screen (CLS_CMD)"},
        "1883": {"comment":"The debug menu"},
        "1892": {"comment":"BREAK?"},
        "1893": {"comment":"0: Status"},
        "1897": {"comment":"1: Memory Browser"},
        "1900": {"comment":"2: Breakpoints"},
        "1904": {"comment":"3: Save 8K Banks"},
        "1908": {"synopsis":"Debug menu 3, Save 8K Banks:\n1. The 64-column screen titled \"Save 8K Banks\" ($1093); the first and last 8K banks asked\n   for (2 hex digits each, below $E0, last not below first); a bad one: a click, DEBUG_MENU.\n2. The file browser ($110F, types FILETYPES_BIN, help HELP_SAVE_BIN), the name (\"Save banks\n   dump as:\"), \"Saving...\".\n3. \".bin\" added when missing (BIN_EXT_TEXT), the file opened, each bank written whole\n   ($1289), the file closed; DEBUG_MENU.\nA DOS error is shown (SAVE_BANKS_ERR) and the file closed.","comment":"Title \"Save 8K Banks\""},
        "1914": {"comment":"\"1st bank:\""},
        "1920": {"comment":"$E0 or more?"},
        "1925": {"comment":"\"last bank:\""},
        "1932": {"comment":"D = the last"},
        "1933": {"comment":"$E0 or more?"},
        "1937": {"comment":"Below the first?"},
        "1941": {"comment":"Back to the normal window"},
        "1944": {"comment":"Choose a .BIN file"},
        "1954": {"comment":"Nothing chosen?"},
        "1957": {"comment":"Ask for the name"},
        "1967": {"comment":"\"Saving...\""},
        "1975": {"comment":"No name?"},
        "1977": {"comment":"\".bin\" added when missing"},
        "1983": {"comment":"Open the file"},
        "1986": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "1988": {"synopsis":"One 8K bank."},
        "1990": {"comment":"Bank E"},
        "1991": {"comment":"Written whole"},
        "1997": {"comment":"Next bank"},
        "1999": {"comment":"Past the last?"},
        "2003": {"comment":"Close the file"},
        "2009": {"synopsis":"Back to the debug menu."},
        "2012": {"synopsis":"No name: error $14.","comment":"Error $14"},
        "2014": {"synopsis":"Shows DOS error A (ROM 0's SHOW_DOS_ERROR), then closes the file ($124B).","comment":"Show the error (SHOW_DOS_ERROR)"},
        "2018": {"comment":"Close the file"},
        "2021": {"synopsis":"A bad bank number: a click, then the debug menu.","comment":"A click (CLICK)"},
        "2024": {"comment":"Back to the debug menu"},
        "2026": {"synopsis":"Debug menu 1, Memory Browser, at address 0 (also key M on the status screen, $0CC6).","comment":"Address 0"},
        "2029": {"synopsis":"The memory browser at address HL (from the status screen, $0CD0).","comment":"Address mode"},
        "2031": {"synopsis":"The memory browser at HL in page C, $FF for address mode (from the breakpoint screen,\n$0F39):\n1. The 64-column screen titled \"Memory Browser\" ($1093), the help MEM_VIEW_HELP; the column\n   numbers 00-0F at row 2 ($1020).\n2. MB_SHOW, then the key loop at $1419 with the key table at $14A1 (cursor MB_CURSOR): 6/7\n   and the cursor keys down/up 256 bytes, 5/8 left/right 8K or a page, EDIT, B, O, A, S, T,\n   F, N, C; SPACE back to the debug menu.\nEntry: HL = the address or offset (L the cursor), C = the page or $FF.","comment":"Position and mode kept"},
        "2033": {"comment":"Title \"Memory Browser\""},
        "2039": {"comment":"The help lines"},
        "2045": {"comment":"16 column numbers from 0"},
        "2048": {"comment":"At row 2, column 8"},
        "2056": {"comment":"The page of bytes"},
        "2059": {"comment":"The browser's keys"},
        "2065": {"synopsis":"Draws the memory browser's page: the header line (MB_HEADER), then from row 3 sixteen rows\nof 16 bytes from HL with L = 0: the row's address or offset, sixteen bytes in hex and\nsixteen characters ('.' for codes outside $20-$7F). In address mode each row's page comes\nfrom the program's MMU copies (ADDR_PAGE); every byte is read through the page cache\n(MAP_PROG_BYTE).\nEntry: HL, C as for MB_AT.\nExit: HL, BC kept.","comment":"The header line"},
        "2068": {"comment":"At row 3, column 0"},
        "2076": {"comment":"From the page's first byte"},
        "2078": {"comment":"16 rows"},
        "2080": {"synopsis":"One row."},
        "2082": {"comment":"Row codes"},
        "2091": {"comment":"The row's address or offset"},
        "2094": {"comment":"Address mode?"},
        "2097": {"comment":"Then A = its page, HL = the offset"},
        "2100": {"comment":"Map the row's bytes"},
        "2106": {"comment":"Codes between"},
        "2115": {"comment":"16 bytes in hex"},
        "2118": {"synopsis":"One byte in hex."},
        "2121": {"comment":"One byte"},
        "2127": {"comment":"Back to the row's first byte"},
        "2134": {"comment":"16 characters"},
        "2136": {"synopsis":"One byte as a character."},
        "2142": {"comment":"End of the row"},
        "2145": {"comment":"The next row's position"},
        "2156": {"synopsis":"Keys 6 and cursor down: 256 bytes on (within the 8K page in bank mode); MB_REDRAW.","comment":"256 bytes on"},
        "2157": {"comment":"Address mode?"},
        "2161": {"comment":"Past the 8K page?"},
        "2165": {"comment":"Then its start"},
        "2167": {"synopsis":"Draws the page again (MB_SHOW); no carry (no click).","comment":"Draw the page"},
        "2170": {"synopsis":"No carry: the key was taken.","comment":"No carry"},
        "2172": {"synopsis":"Keys 7 and cursor up: 256 bytes back (within the 8K page in bank mode); MB_REDRAW.","comment":"256 bytes back"},
        "2173": {"comment":"Address mode?"},
        "2177": {"comment":"Below the 8K page?"},
        "2181": {"comment":"Then its last 256"},
        "2185": {"synopsis":"Keys 5 and cursor left: the previous page ($DF after 0) in bank mode, 8K back in address\nmode; MB_REDRAW.","comment":"Address mode?"},
        "2189": {"comment":"The previous page"},
        "2192": {"comment":"Below 0?"},
        "2194": {"comment":"Then the last, $DF"},
        "2198": {"synopsis":"Address mode: 8K back.","comment":"8K back"},
        "2204": {"synopsis":"Keys 8 and cursor right: the next page (0 after $DF) in bank mode, 8K on in address mode;\nMB_REDRAW.","comment":"Address mode?"},
        "2208": {"comment":"The next page"},
        "2209": {"comment":"Past $DF?"},
        "2214": {"comment":"Then 0"},
        "2218": {"synopsis":"Address mode: 8K on.","comment":"8K on"},
        "2224": {"synopsis":"Key B: asks \"bank:\" (2 hex digits, $0B0F); below $E0 the browser shows that page at the same\noffset (bank mode); otherwise carry (a click).","comment":"\"bank:\""},
        "2230": {"comment":"$E0 or more: carry"},
        "2234": {"comment":"C = the page"},
        "2235": {"comment":"The offset within it"},
        "2241": {"synopsis":"Key O, bank mode only: asks \"offset:\" (4 hex digits, $0B16); below $2000 it becomes the\nposition; otherwise carry.","comment":"Address mode: carry"},
        "2245": {"comment":"\"offset:\""},
        "2251": {"comment":"$2000 or more: carry"},
        "2256": {"comment":"HL = the offset"},
        "2259": {"synopsis":"Key A: asks \"address:\" (4 hex digits) and shows it in address mode.","comment":"\"address:\""},
        "2265": {"comment":"HL = the address"},
        "2266": {"comment":"Address mode"},
        "2270": {"synopsis":"Key EDIT: hex editing from the cursor: each byte typed (2 hex digits, $0B58) is written to\nthe program's memory (MB_POKE) and shown as a character; after 2 digits the cursor moves on;\nENTER with no digit, or after one, ends it (MB_KEY_OK or return)."},
        "2272": {"comment":"2 hex digits"},
        "2280": {"comment":"None typed: done"},
        "2285": {"comment":"Write the byte"},
        "2288": {"comment":"At its character"},
        "2291": {"comment":"Shown as a character"},
        "2297": {"comment":"Ended by ENTER?"},
        "2298": {"comment":"Next byte"},
        "2299": {"comment":"Header for the new position"},
        "2302": {"comment":"Cursor to its hex digits"},
        "2310": {"synopsis":"Key T: text editing from the cursor: each key typed (MB_READ_KEY) is written to the\nprogram's memory and shown in hex; ENTER ends it.","comment":"At the byte's character"},
        "2313": {"comment":"A key; ENTER?"},
