        "3011": {"comment":"All digits typed: carry, NZ"},
        "3012": {"comment":"A = $FF"},
        "3014": {"synopsis":"Entered from $031F (after an NMI, A = the old $3F2D with bit 0 set) and $0364 ('D' on the\nerror screen, A = 'D'). Unless A = $FF, finds whether the NMI came from a breakpoint:\n1. Each of the 20 slots (BP_RECORD) that is enabled is compared with the NMI return address\n   at $3F9F (the copy of NextRegs $C2-$C3) as page and offset ($0047).\n2. When the PC lies 4 bytes past a slot's offset in its page - just after the 4-byte NEXTREG\n   $02,$08 that generated the NMI - $3F9F goes back by 4, onto the breakpoint.\n3. On to STATUS_SCREEN.","comment":"A = $FF: no breakpoint check"},
        "3015": {"comment":"Yes: straight to the Status screen"},
        "3017": {"comment":"20 breakpoint slots"},
        "3019": {"synopsis":"One slot.","comment":"Slot counter kept"},
        "3020": {"comment":"Slot enabled?"},
        "3023": {"comment":"No: next slot"},
        "3025": {"comment":"HL = its offset + 4: past the 4-byte patch"},
        "3029": {"comment":"The slot's page kept"},
        "3031": {"comment":"PC's page and offset (the NMI return address)"},
        "3034": {"comment":"A = its page, HL = its offset"},
        "3037": {"comment":"DE = the slot's offset + 4"},
        "3038": {"comment":"B = the slot's page"},
        "3039": {"comment":"PC 4 past this slot's offset?"},
        "3042": {"comment":"No: next slot"},
        "3044": {"comment":"In the slot's page?"},
        "3045": {"comment":"No: next slot"},
        "3047": {"comment":"PC back by 4: on the breakpoint"},
        "3050": {"comment":"- 4"},
        "3054": {"comment":"Stored back"},
        "3057": {"comment":"Status screen"},
        "3058": {"comment":"Slot found: the Status screen"},
        "3060": {"synopsis":"The next slot.","comment":"Next slot"},
        "3061": {"comment":"20 slots"},
        "3063": {"comment":"None hit"},
        "3065": {"synopsis":"Key 'S' in the memory browser's and the breakpoint screen's key tables ($14A1, $14D7): the\nkey loop's return address and table pointer dropped, then STATUS_SCREEN.","comment":"The key loop's return and table dropped"},
        "3066": {"comment":"Table pointer dropped"},
        "3067": {"synopsis":"The Status screen (Debug menu item 0, from $0766):\n1. The hi-res screen titled 'Status' (HIRES_SCREEN with $10DB).\n2. The register names ($1D33) and the help, OS and 'Core ' texts ($1DF9).\n3. The core version from NextRegs $01 and $0E as major.minor.sub.\n4. The numbers of the NextRegs in NEXTREG_LIST in inverse: 28 on line 0, 28 on line 2, 25 on\n   line 4.\n5. '-->' at column 10 of each line in ARROW_LINES.\n6. Every item of REG_LAYOUT shown (REG_SHOW).\n7. KEY_LOOP with the keys at REG_KEYS, the cursor on the first item (HL = REG_LAYOUT, C =\n   0).","comment":"Hi-res screen titled 'Status'"},
        "3070": {"comment":"HIRES_SCREEN"},
        "3073": {"comment":"Register names"},
        "3076": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "3079": {"comment":"Help line, OS version and 'Core '"},
        "3082": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "3085": {"comment":"Core version: NextReg $01"},
        "3087": {"comment":"READ_NEXTREG"},
        "3090": {"comment":"C kept"},
        "3091": {"comment":"Major (high nibble)"},
        "3093": {"comment":"Printed as a hex digit"},
        "3096": {"comment":"'.', then the minor (low nibble) in decimal"},
        "3099": {"comment":"The minor version"},
        "3102": {"comment":"2 decimal digits"},
        "3105": {"comment":"'.', then NextReg $0E in decimal"},
        "3110": {"comment":"READ_NEXTREG"},
