        "3376": {"comment":"PRINT_BYTE_AT"},
        "3380": {"comment":"A = the byte"},
        "3381": {"comment":"Line pointer back"},
        "3382": {"comment":"Shown in binary too (kind bit 4)?"},
        "3384": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "3385": {"comment":"A space"},
        "3389": {"comment":"A = the byte"},
        "3390": {"comment":"8 bits, the top one first"},
        "3392": {"synopsis":"One bit.","comment":"Top bit into carry"},
        "3394": {"comment":"'0' or '1'"},
        "3396": {"comment":"+ carry"},
        "3398": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "3400": {"comment":"8 bits"},
        "3403": {"synopsis":"The Status screen's cursor routine (REG_KEYS's first word, called by KEY_LOOP): AT the item,\none place back, and the text at DE there ('>' in inverse, or a space).","comment":"AT the item"},
        "3404": {"comment":"REG_AT"},
        "3407": {"comment":"Code 8: one place back, before the value"},
        "3409": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "3410": {"comment":"The cursor text at DE"},
        "3411": {"comment":"PRINT_TEXT_DE"},
        "3414": {"synopsis":"Item C of the line at HL in REG_LAYOUT: prints AT its line and column, and gives its kind\nand slot.\nEntry: HL = the line's header, C = the item.\nExit: D = the kind - low nibble the hex digits; bit 6 item 0, bit 7 another item, bit 5 a\nword, bit 4 shown in binary too: $42 or $64 for item 0 (without or with the column's bit 7),\n$82 or $92 for the others; E = the slot's low byte ($3F00 + E). Keeps BC, HL.","comment":"Item kept"},
        "3415": {"comment":"Line pointer kept"},
        "3416": {"comment":"D = the line number"},
        "3419": {"comment":"HL = item C's two bytes"},
        "3421": {"comment":"2 bytes an item"},
        "3423": {"comment":"E = its column (bit 7 a flag), B = its slot"},
        "3424": {"comment":"Next byte"},
        "3425": {"comment":"B = the slot byte"},
        "3426": {"comment":"AT the line, the column without bit 7"},
        "3427": {"comment":"Without its flag"},
        "3429": {"comment":"AT the line, that column"},
        "3433": {"comment":"D = the column byte, E = the slot"},
        "3434": {"comment":"E = the slot's low byte"},
        "3435": {"comment":"Line pointer back"},
        "3436": {"comment":"Item back"},
        "3437": {"comment":"Item 0?"},
        "3440": {"comment":"Kind $C2: 2 digits"},
        "3442": {"comment":"Item other than 0"},
        "3444": {"comment":"Item 0 with bit 7: kind $E4, a word (4 digits)"},
        "3445": {"comment":"Bit 7 clear: a byte"},
        "3447": {"comment":"Bit 7 set: a word"},
        "3449": {"synopsis":"Item 0: bit 7 of the kind cleared.","comment":"C is 0 here, so no return"},
        "3451": {"comment":"Never taken"},
        "3452": {"comment":"Item 0's kind: bit 7 cleared ($42 or $64)"},
        "3455": {"synopsis":"Another item: kind $82, or $92 with the column's bit 7.","comment":"Other items: $82"},
        "3457": {"comment":"Bit 7: $92, shown in binary too"},
        "3458": {"comment":"No flag: done"},
        "3459": {"comment":"Kind $92"},
        "3462": {"synopsis":"The Status screen's layout, read by $0C60, REG_NEXT_LINE, REG_KEY_UP and REG_AT: 16 lines,\neach a header byte (bits 0-5 the item count, bit 6 another line follows, bit 7 a line comes\nbefore), the screen line, then 2 bytes an item: the column (bit 7 a flag, see REG_AT) and\nthe low byte of its slot at $3Fxx. Lines 1, 3 and 5 hold the 81 NextReg copies from $3F4E;\nlines 7-20 the registers saved by the NMI code, words in column 5 (the PC from $3F9F on line\n20)."},
        "3702": {"synopsis":"The 83 NextRegs whose values are kept at $3F4E-$3FA0, in that order, ended by 0: read by\n$179A and $17B1 and, for their numbers on the Status screen, by STATUS_SCREEN (the first\n81). $50-$57 land at $3F6A-$3F71 (the MMU), $C2-$C3 at $3F9F-$3FA0 (the NMI return address)."},
        "3786": {"synopsis":"The Status screen's lines that get '-->' after their word register: 7, 8, 9, 11, 12, 13, 15,\n16, 18, 20; bit 7 marks the last. Read by STATUS_SCREEN."},
        "3796": {"synopsis":"Key 'B' on the Status screen (REG_KEYS): the key loop's return address and table pointer\ndropped, then BP_SCREEN.","comment":"The key loop's return and table dropped"},
        "3797": {"comment":"Table pointer dropped"},
        "3798": {"synopsis":"The Breakpoints screen (Debug menu item 2, from $076D):\n1. The hi-res screen titled 'Breakpoints' and its help ($1E91).\n2. For the 20 slots: the number in inverse, then BP_SHOW_SLOT; a new line each.\n3. The global state at 0,71 (BP_SHOW_GLOBAL).\n4. KEY_LOOP with the keys at BP_KEYS, the cursor on slot 0 (B = 20; the slot is 20 - B).","comment":"Hi-res screen titled 'Breakpoints'"},
        "3801": {"comment":"HIRES_SCREEN"},
        "3804": {"comment":"Help line"},
        "3807": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "3810": {"comment":"20 slots, one a line"},
