        "4243": {"synopsis":"Sets up the debugger's screen:\n1. Port $FF = 6 (Timex hi-res) with ATTR_P's bits 3-5 inverted; $5C7F (IY+$45) = 9.\n2. Channels K and S given the routine $5B4D (SET_SCREEN_CHAN).\n3. $3F30 = $FB00: RST $30 prints in that window.\n4. Code $0E, the title (SHOW_TITLE), then codes $1A 0 and $1E 6.\nEntry: HL = the title, ended by a control code.","comment":"Title kept"},
        "4244": {"comment":"Port $FF = 6 (hi-res) + ATTR_P's bits 3-5 inverted"},
        "4247": {"comment":"Paper bits inverted"},
        "4248": {"comment":"Bits 3-5"},
        "4250": {"comment":"+ 6: hi-res"},
        "4252": {"comment":"Timex screen mode port"},
        "4254": {"comment":"$5C7F = 9"},
        "4258": {"comment":"Channels K and S through $5B4D"},
        "4261": {"comment":"SET_SCREEN_CHAN"},
        "4264": {"comment":"RST $30 prints in the window at $FB00"},
        "4267": {"comment":"RST $30's window"},
        "4270": {"comment":"HL = the title"},
        "4271": {"comment":"Code $0E: the window cleared"},
        "4273": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "4274": {"comment":"The title bar"},
        "4277": {"comment":"Code $1A, 0: no pauses"},
        "4279": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "4280": {"comment":"Its parameter, 0"},
        "4281": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "4282": {"comment":"Code $1E, 6"},
        "4284": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "4285": {"comment":"Its parameter, 6"},
        "4287": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "4289": {"synopsis":"Back to the standard screen: port $FF = 0, $5C7F = 0, channels K and S given the routine\n$09F4 (SET_SCREEN_CHAN), then WINDOW_F700.","comment":"Port $FF = 0: the standard screen"},
        "4290": {"comment":"Timex screen mode port"},
        "4292": {"comment":"$5C7F = 0"},
        "4295": {"comment":"Channels K and S back to $09F4"},
        "4298": {"synopsis":"Channels K and S get the routine BC, by ROM 1's SM_CHANNELS ($144F) with carry set; then\nWINDOW_F700.","comment":"Carry set"},
        "4299": {"comment":"Channels K and S get routine BC"},
        "4302": {"synopsis":"$3F30 = $F700: RST $30 prints in that window. Also from $032F.","comment":"RST $30 prints in the window at $F700"},
        "4305": {"comment":"RST $30's window"},
        "4309": {"synopsis":"The Debug menu's text, $3A bytes to $110E, copied to PROG by SHOW_MENU_TEXT (from $075B):\nthe title 'Debug' and four items, each ended by $0D; the character before a '_' is an item's\nhotkey. The items are also the titles of their screens (MENU_TXT_STATUS ...)."},
        "4315": {"synopsis":"'S_tatus': item 0, also the Status screen's title ($0BFB)."},
        "4323": {"synopsis":"'M_emory Browser': item 1, also its screen's title ($07F1)."},
        "4339": {"synopsis":"'B_reakpoints': item 2, also its screen's title ($0ED6)."},
        "4352": {"synopsis":"'Save 8K_ Banks': item 3, also its screen's title ($0774)."},
        "4367": {"synopsis":"Runs the file browser to choose a file to save to:\n1. $3E97 = 0.\n2. The file types at HL and the help at BC expanded to $5F00 and $5F80 (EXPAND_TEXT).\n3. RESET_STREAMS.\n4. Capabilities: none when $05C5 gives B = 2, otherwise CAPS2 ($40) with B = $08 (sorting).\n5. ROM 0's IDE_BROWSER.\nEntry: HL = the file types, BC = the help.\nExit: carry, Z: a file chosen, HL = its long name, DE = its short one; NZ: none, with carry\nunless BREAK (CAPS SHIFT and SPACE) is held.","comment":"$3E97 = 0: no enMf .sys file kept"},
        "4368": {"comment":"$3E97"},
        "4371": {"comment":"File types expanded to $5F00"},
