        "5145": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "5149": {"synopsis":"Shows the menu at PROG again, with the item selected last time ($F700). Not called from\nanywhere in the ROM.","comment":"Item selected last time"},
        "5152": {"comment":"Shown"},
        "5154": {"synopsis":"The key loop of the debugger's screens.\nEntry: DE = a key table, HL and BC = the screen's state (its cursor).\n1. The table's first word, the cursor routine, called with DE = $1C24 ('>' in inverse).\n2. A key (ROM 0's WAIT_KEY_CLICK); the cursor routine again with DE = $1CD6 (a space).\n3. Space: on to $0755, the Debug menu.\n4. Letters made capitals; the key looked up in the 3-byte entries after the first word (key,\n   routine word), up to $FF. Found: the routine run with HL and BC, which it returns\n   changed; carry means refused.\n5. A refused or unknown key: a click. Again from 1. Tables: REG_KEYS, MEM_KEYS, BP_KEYS.","comment":"Keeps the table and the state"},
        "5155": {"comment":"State kept"},
        "5157": {"comment":"IX = the cursor routine (the table's first word)"},
        "5164": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "5166": {"comment":"Cursor drawn: '>' in inverse"},
        "5172": {"comment":"Wait for a key"},
        "5175": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "5177": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "5178": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "5179": {"comment":"State kept again"},
        "5181": {"comment":"The key kept"},
        "5182": {"comment":"Cursor erased: a space"},
        "5188": {"comment":"The key"},
        "5189": {"comment":"DE = the saved HL"},
        "5190": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "5191": {"comment":"HL = the table"},
        "5192": {"comment":"Space: back to the Debug menu"},
        "5194": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "5197": {"comment":"Table kept"},
        "5198": {"comment":"Lower-case letters made capitals"},
        "5200": {"comment":"Below 'a'"},
        "5204": {"comment":"Above 'z'"},
        "5206": {"comment":"Capitals"},
        "5208": {"synopsis":"The next entry.","comment":"Next entry: key, routine word"},
        "5209": {"comment":"Past the routine word"},
        "5210": {"comment":"End ($FF)?"},
        "5212": {"comment":"Yes: unknown key"},
        "5214": {"comment":"This key?"},
        "5215": {"comment":"Past the key"},
        "5216": {"comment":"No: next entry"},
        "5218": {"comment":"DE = its routine"},
        "5219": {"comment":"Next byte"},
        "5221": {"comment":"HL = the routine"},
        "5222": {"comment":"HL = the state, DE = the routine"},
        "5223": {"comment":"Run it; carry: refused"},
        "5226": {"comment":"DE = the table"},
        "5227": {"comment":"Carry: refused"},
        "5229": {"comment":"Next key"},
        "5231": {"synopsis":"No entry for the key.","comment":"Unknown key: HL = the state"},
        "5232": {"comment":"DE = the table"},
        "5233": {"synopsis":"A click (ROM 0's $3E18).","comment":"Refused: a click"},
        "5236": {"comment":"A click"},
        "5239": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "5240": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "5241": {"comment":"DE back"},
        "5242": {"comment":"Next key"},
        "5244": {"synopsis":"Jumps to IX: the cursor routine.","comment":"The cursor routine"},
        "5246": {"synopsis":"Jumps to DE: a key's routine.","comment":"Jumps to DE"},
        "5247": {"comment":"RET to it"},
        "5248": {"synopsis":"The Status screen's key table for KEY_LOOP: the cursor routine REG_CURSOR, then key and\nroutine: '6' and $0A REG_KEY_DOWN, '7' and $0B REG_KEY_UP, '5' and 8 REG_KEY_LEFT, '8' and 9\nREG_KEY_RIGHT, $07 REG_KEY_EDIT, 'B' BP_FROM_KEY, 'C' $03EE, 'M' REG_KEY_MEMORY, 'V' $03A9;\n$FF."},
        "5290": {"synopsis":"The memory browser's key table for KEY_LOOP (from $080B): the cursor routine $0AF4, then '6'\nand $0A $086C, '7' and $0B $087C, '5' and 8 $0889, '8' and 9 $089C, $07 $08DE, 'B' $08B0,\n'O' $08C1, 'A' $08D3, 'S' STATUS_FROM_KEY, 'T' $0906, 'F' $092A, 'N' $09B1, 'C' $09BC; $FF."},
        "5344": {"synopsis":"The Breakpoint screen's key table for KEY_LOOP: the cursor routine BP_CURSOR, then '6' and\n$0A BP_KEY_DOWN, '7' and $0B BP_KEY_UP, 'S' STATUS_FROM_KEY, 'C' $03EE, 'K' BP_KEY_KILL, 'D'\nBP_KEY_DISABLE, 'E' BP_KEY_ENABLE, 'G' BP_KEY_GLOBAL, 'M' BP_KEY_MEMORY, 'B' BP_KEY_BANK,\n'A' BP_KEY_ADDRESS; $FF."},
        "5386": {"synopsis":"The NMI menu's text, $57 bytes to $1557, copied to PROG by NMI_MENU: the title 'NMI Menu'\nand eight items, each ended by $0D, the character before a '_' an item's hotkey: Snapshot,\nScreenshot, TAP Files, POKEs, Debug Tools, Settings, Keymap, About."},
        "5473": {"synopsis":"RST $10's second half (from $0015: BC kept at $5B54, HL = the address of the word after the\nRST, the caller's HL on the stack): calls the address in that word with the Multiface paged\nout and returns past the word with it paged in again. RAM_MF_IN ($5C23) and the address are\nstacked and RAM_MF_OUT ($5C1C) entered; no ROM is selected, so the address runs in the ROM\nselected already (ROM 0). BC reaches it; AF comes back from it.","comment":"BC = the word after the RST: the address"},
        "5474": {"comment":"Next byte"},
        "5476": {"comment":"Past the word"},
        "5477": {"comment":"Return past the word; HL back"},
        "5478": {"comment":"Way back: RAM_MF_IN ($5C23) pages the Multiface in"},
        "5482": {"comment":"The address to go to"},
        "5483": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "5487": {"comment":"RAM_MF_OUT ($5C1C) pages it out, then RET to it"},
        "5490": {"synopsis":"Makes the RST $08 call whose code is the byte after the CALL: the byte stored at $5B5E,\nafter the RST $08 of RAM_ERROR_STUB ($5B5D), which is then called in ROM 3 by RST $28. Used\nwith $86 (DISK_STRMSTART), $87 (DISK_STRMEND) and $92 (M_DRVAPI).\nExit: past the byte, with the call's results.","comment":"HL = the byte after the CALL"},
        "5491": {"comment":"AF kept"},
        "5492": {"comment":"The byte into $5B5E, after RAM_ERROR_STUB's RST $08"},
        "5494": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "5497": {"comment":"AF back"},
        "5498": {"comment":"Return past the byte"},
        "5499": {"comment":"RST $08 with it, at $5B5D with ROM 3"},
        "5503": {"synopsis":"RST $18's second half (from $001D): as CALL_ROM0_TAIL, with RAM_ROM1 ($5B3E) stacked to\nselect ROM 1 first and RAM_ROM0 ($5B4D) to select ROM 0 on the way back.","comment":"BC = the word after the RST: the address"},
        "5504": {"comment":"Next byte"},
        "5506": {"comment":"Past the word"},
        "5507": {"comment":"Return past the word; HL back"},
        "5508": {"comment":"Way back: RAM_MF_IN ($5C23) pages the Multiface in"},
        "5512": {"comment":"Before that, RAM_ROM0 ($5B4D)"},
        "5516": {"comment":"The address to go to"},
        "5517": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "5521": {"comment":"First RAM_ROM1 ($5B3E)"},
        "5525": {"comment":"RAM_MF_OUT ($5C1C) pages it out, then RET"},
        "5528": {"synopsis":"RST $20's second half (from $0025): as CALL_ROM1_TAIL, with RAM_ROM2 ($5B43) selecting ROM\n2.","comment":"BC = the word after the RST: the address"},
        "5529": {"comment":"Next byte"},
        "5531": {"comment":"Past the word"},
        "5532": {"comment":"Return past the word; HL back"},
        "5533": {"comment":"Way back: RAM_MF_IN ($5C23) pages the Multiface in"},
        "5537": {"comment":"Before that, RAM_ROM0 ($5B4D)"},
        "5541": {"comment":"The address to go to"},
        "5542": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "5546": {"comment":"First RAM_ROM2 ($5B43)"},
        "5550": {"comment":"RAM_MF_OUT ($5C1C) pages it out, then RET"},
        "5553": {"synopsis":"RST $28's second half (from $002D): as CALL_ROM1_TAIL, with RAM_ROM3 ($5B48) selecting ROM\n3.","comment":"BC = the word after the RST: the address"},
        "5554": {"comment":"Next byte"},
        "5556": {"comment":"Past the word"},
        "5557": {"comment":"Return past the word; HL back"},
        "5558": {"comment":"Way back: RAM_MF_IN ($5C23) pages the Multiface in"},
        "5562": {"comment":"Before that, RAM_ROM0 ($5B4D)"},
        "5566": {"comment":"The address to go to"},
        "5567": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "5571": {"comment":"First RAM_ROM3 ($5B48)"},
        "5575": {"comment":"RAM_MF_OUT ($5C1C) pages it out, then RET"},
        "5578": {"synopsis":"Reads the word at address HL of the interrupted program's memory, each byte through its page\nunder the saved MMU ($0047) and MAP_PROG_BYTE.\nExit: HL = the word, A = its high byte. From $05D5 and $05DC.","comment":"Page and offset of HL"},
        "5579": {"comment":"A = the page, HL = the offset"},
        "5582": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "5585": {"comment":"Low byte"},
        "5586": {"comment":"Address back, + 1"},
        "5588": {"comment":"Page and offset"},
        "5591": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "5594": {"comment":"High byte"},
        "5595": {"comment":"L = the low byte"},
        "5596": {"comment":"HL = the word"},
        "5598": {"synopsis":"Writes DE at address HL of the interrupted program's memory, each byte paged in like\nPEEK_WORD and its page marked changed (CACHE_DIRTY). Not called from anywhere in the ROM.","comment":"Not called from anywhere in the ROM"},
        "5600": {"comment":"Address paged in"},
        "5603": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "5606": {"comment":"E = the low byte"},
        "5607": {"comment":"E written"},
        "5608": {"comment":"Page marked changed ($3F34 = 1)"},
        "5611": {"comment":"HL = the address"},
        "5613": {"comment":"Next address"},
        "5614": {"comment":"Page and offset"},
        "5617": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "5620": {"comment":"D = the high byte"},
        "5621": {"comment":"D written"},
        "5622": {"comment":"Marked changed"},
        "5625": {"synopsis":"A = 2 x the 128K/+3 ROM selected in the saved paging: bit 2 from the $1FFD copy at $3FFF,\nbit 1 from bit 4 of the $7FFD copy at $3FCC.\nChanges: B. From $01F1 and $1629.","comment":"B = the port $1FFD copy"},
        "5629": {"comment":"Port $7FFD copy: its bit 4 to bit 1"},
        "5632": {"comment":"Bit 4 to bit 1"},
        "5635": {"comment":"$1FFD's bit 1 cleared"},
        "5637": {"comment":"A = the ROM x 2: bit 2 from $1FFD, bit 1 from $7FFD"},
        "5638": {"comment":"Bits 1-2 only"},
        "5641": {"synopsis":"Maps a byte of the interrupted program's memory so that the Multiface can read or write it.\nThe program's 8K pages are where it left them, except those the Multiface uses itself, which\nit moved before running: page $0A to DivMMC bank 6, page $10 to bank 11, pages $0E/$0F to\nbanks 4/5 (RAM_SNAP_SAVE), and the first $1800 bytes of page $0B to the Multiface RAM at\n$2000 ($02B8).\n1. A ROM slot ($FF) is read from the program's ROM, a moved page from its copy, both through\n   a 256-byte cache at $5E00. Any other page (and page $0B from offset $1800) is paged into\n   $8000-$9FFF with MMU 4 and used there (MAP_VIA_MMU4).\n2. The cache's source is kept at $3F32 (its key: $86/$8B/$84/$85 a DivMMC bank with CONMEM,\n   $00 the Multiface RAM, 1/3/5/7 ROM 0-3; $FF nothing cached) and $3F33 (the offset's high\n   byte); a hit returns at once (MAP_CACHED).\n3. Otherwise the cache is written back (CACHE_FLUSH) and the 256-byte block holding the byte\n   is copied to $5E00 (MAP_CACHE_FILL). $15C1 and $15D5 read and write a word through this\n   routine.\nEntry: A = the slot's 8K page ($FF a ROM) and E = the low byte of its entry in the page\ntable at $3F6A ($6B for slot 1), as $0047 leaves them; HL = the offset in the slot\n($0000-$1FFF).\nExit: HL = where the byte is now. A writer into the cache calls CACHE_DIRTY.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE.","comment":"ROM in this slot?"},
        "5645": {"comment":"Pages below $0A are used through MMU 4"},
        "5651": {"comment":"Page $0B?"},
        "5655": {"comment":"Page $10? Pages above it go through MMU 4"},
        "5661": {"comment":"Page $0E?"},
        "5665": {"comment":"Page $0F?"},
        "5669": {"synopsis":"Pages the 8K page A in with MMU 4 and returns HL in $8000-$9FFF.","comment":"Page it in at $8000-$9FFF"},
        "5672": {"comment":"HL = the byte there"},
        "5675": {"synopsis":"A ROM slot: the cache key is 2 x the program's ROM number + 1; slot 1 reads the ROM's upper\n8K.","comment":"Slot 1 ($2000-$3FFF)?"},
        "5680": {"comment":"Then the ROM's upper 8K"},
        "5682": {"synopsis":"Cache key of the program's ROM (2 x its number + 1).","comment":"A = 2 x the program's ROM"},
        "5685": {"comment":"Odd: a ROM's key"},
        "5688": {"synopsis":"Page $0A: its copy in DivMMC bank 6 ($86).","comment":"DivMMC bank 6"},
        "5692": {"synopsis":"Page $0B: below offset $1800 its copy in the Multiface RAM (key $00); from $1800 the page\nitself through MMU 4.","comment":"Offset $1800 or more?"},
        "5697": {"comment":"Yes: page $0B itself"},
        "5701": {"synopsis":"Key $00: the Multiface RAM.","comment":"No: the copy in the Multiface RAM"},
        "5704": {"synopsis":"Page $10: its copy in DivMMC bank 11 ($8B).","comment":"DivMMC bank 11"},
        "5708": {"synopsis":"Page $0E: its copy in DivMMC bank 4 ($84).","comment":"DivMMC bank 4"},
        "5712": {"synopsis":"Page $0F: its copy in DivMMC bank 5 ($85).","comment":"DivMMC bank 5"},
        "5714": {"synopsis":"Looks the key A and the high byte H up in the cache: on a hit HL is moved into $5E00-$5EFF.","comment":"E = the cached key, D = its high byte"},
        "5718": {"comment":"Same key?"},
        "5722": {"comment":"Same 256 bytes?"},
        "5727": {"comment":"Hit: HL = the byte in the cache"},
        "5730": {"synopsis":"Cache miss: writes the old block back, notes the new key and high byte at $3F32, and copies\nthe 256-byte block (offset H*256) to $5E00 by the key's kind.","comment":"Write the old block back first"},
        "5737": {"comment":"Note the new key and high byte"},
        "5743": {"comment":"The 256-byte block holding the byte"},
        "5752": {"comment":"DivMMC bank?"},
        "5756": {"comment":"Copy it from $2000 + offset"},
        "5761": {"synopsis":"HL = the byte's address in the cache."},
        "5765": {"synopsis":"Key $00 copies straight from the Multiface RAM at $2000 + offset; a ROM key goes on to\nMAP_FILL_ROM.","comment":"ROM?"},
        "5767": {"comment":"No: copy from the Multiface RAM"},
        "5773": {"synopsis":"ROM key: patches RAM_ROM_LDIR's restart to RST $10/$18/$20/$28 for ROM 0-3 and runs the copy\nwith that ROM paged in, under the program's alternate-ROM setting (NextReg $8C from $3F89).","comment":"RST $10/$18/$20/$28 for ROM 0-3"},
        "5779": {"comment":"Patch the restart at $5B73"},
        "5782": {"comment":"The program's alternate-ROM setting"},
        "5788": {"comment":"Copy the block from that ROM"},
        "5791": {"comment":"Alternate ROM off again"},
        "5797": {"synopsis":"Writes the 256-byte cache at $5E00 back to its source if it was written to.\n1. Returns if the flag at $3F34 is clear; clears it.\n2. Returns if nothing is cached ($3F32 = $FF) or the source is a ROM.\n3. Copies $5E00 back to $2000 + offset in the DivMMC bank (through $5CA0) or the Multiface\n   RAM.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Cache written to?"},
        "5802": {"comment":"Not any more"},
        "5806": {"comment":"E = the key, D = the high byte"},
        "5811": {"comment":"Nothing cached?"},
        "5814": {"comment":"DE = $2000 + offset"},
        "5824": {"comment":"DivMMC bank: copy back through $5CA0"},
        "5828": {"comment":"ROM: nothing to write"},
        "5829": {"comment":"Multiface RAM: copy back"},
        "5832": {"synopsis":"Marks the cache at $5E00 as written to ($3F34 = 1).\nChanges: A."},
        "5838": {"synopsis":"Empties the cache: not written to, no source ($3F32 = $FF).\nChanges: A."},
        "5847": {"synopsis":"Copies 4 bytes between the interrupted program's memory and a buffer, one byte at a time\nthrough MAP_PROG_BYTE.\nEntry: A = the 8K page, HL = the offset in it, DE = the buffer; carry set copies from the\nprogram to the buffer, carry clear from the buffer to the program.\nExit: HL and DE moved on by 4. A writer calls CACHE_DIRTY afterwards.\nChanges: F (and the cache).","comment":"4 bytes"},
        "5849": {"synopsis":"One byte."},
        "5853": {"comment":"HL = where the byte is now"},
        "5859": {"comment":"Carry: from the program to DE"},
        "5861": {"comment":"No carry: from DE to the program"},
        "5862": {"synopsis":"Copies the byte."},
        "5867": {"comment":"Next byte on both sides"},
        "5872": {"synopsis":"Reads breakpoint record 20 - B. The 20 records of 7 bytes start at $3EA1: a word (the offset\nin the 8K page, bit 15 set when the breakpoint is in use, bit 14 a further flag), the 8K\npage, and the 4 program bytes the breakpoint replaced.\nEntry: B = 20 down to 1.\nExit: DE = the offset without the flag bits, A = the page, C = the word's high byte with the\nflags, HL = the record's 4 saved bytes; zero flag set when the record is not in use.\nChanges: F, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Record number 0-19"},
        "5878": {"comment":"7 bytes a record"},
        "5881": {"comment":"HL = the record"},
        "5885": {"comment":"DE = the offset with the flags"},
        "5889": {"comment":"A = the 8K page"},
        "5891": {"comment":"C = the flags"},
        "5892": {"comment":"Offset without the flag bits"},
        "5896": {"comment":"In use?"},
        "5899": {"synopsis":"Removes the planted breakpoints from the program, if bit 7 of $3F2E says they are planted\n(and clears it). For each record in use:\n1. Reads the 4 bytes at the breakpoint.\n2. If they are still BP_INSTRUCTION, puts the saved bytes back; otherwise the program\n   overwrote them and the record is marked not in use.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Breakpoints planted?"},
        "5905": {"comment":"Not any more"},
        "5907": {"comment":"20 records"},
        "5909": {"synopsis":"One record."},
        "5910": {"comment":"Skip a record not in use"},
        "5915": {"comment":"HL = the offset, DE = the saved bytes"},
        "5919": {"comment":"Read the 4 bytes now at the breakpoint"},
        "5928": {"comment":"Still the breakpoint instruction?"},
        "5933": {"synopsis":"Compares one byte with BP_INSTRUCTION."},
        "5941": {"synopsis":"A = the page, HL = the offset; the zero flag holds the comparison.","comment":"A = the page"},
        "5946": {"comment":"Overwritten: record no longer in use"},
        "5953": {"synopsis":"Writes the saved bytes back over the breakpoint.","comment":"DE = the saved bytes"},
        "5954": {"comment":"Write them back"},
        "5958": {"comment":"Cache written to"},
        "5961": {"synopsis":"Next record."},
        "5965": {"synopsis":"Plants the breakpoints in the program before it resumes, unless bit 6 of $3F2E is set; sets\nbit 7 of $3F2E. For each record in use:\n1. If the breakpoint is in the 8K page of the program's PC (the word at $3F9F) and the PC\n   lies from the breakpoint to 6 bytes past it, the record is marked not in use instead.\n2. Otherwise saves the 4 program bytes in the record and writes BP_INSTRUCTION over them.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Breakpoints switched off?"},
        "5971": {"comment":"Mark them as planted"},
        "5973": {"comment":"20 records"},
        "5975": {"synopsis":"One record."},
        "5976": {"comment":"Skip a record not in use"},
        "5984": {"comment":"A = the page of the program's PC"},
        "5992": {"comment":"Breakpoint in the PC's page?"},
        "5996": {"comment":"PC more than 6 bytes past it?"},
        "6003": {"comment":"PC before it?"},
        "6007": {"comment":"PC on it: record no longer in use"},
        "6014": {"synopsis":"Saves the 4 bytes and writes BP_INSTRUCTION in their place.","comment":"DE = the save area, HL = the offset"},
        "6016": {"comment":"Save the program's 4 bytes"},
        "6024": {"comment":"Write the breakpoint instruction"},
        "6031": {"comment":"Cache written to"},
        "6034": {"synopsis":"Next record."},
        "6038": {"synopsis":"The breakpoint instruction, NEXTREG $02,$08 (ED 91 02 08): written over the program's code,\nit makes the Multiface's NMI (NextReg $02 bit 3). Read by BP_REMOVE_ALL and BP_PLANT_ALL;\nnever run here."},
        "6042": {"synopsis":"Reads a NextReg.\nEntry: A = the register.\nExit: A = its value, BC = $253B.\nChanges: AF, BC.","comment":"Select the register"},
        "6047": {"comment":"Read its value"},
        "6051": {"synopsis":"Saves the NextRegs listed at $0E76 (0-ended) to $3F4E onwards.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Values to $3F4E"},
        "6054": {"comment":"Register numbers from $0E76"},
        "6060": {"synopsis":"One register.","comment":"Next register; 0 ends"},
        "6064": {"comment":"Select it"},
        "6067": {"comment":"Read and store its value"},
        "6074": {"synopsis":"Writes the NextRegs listed at $0E76 back from $3F4E, all but $8F (RESTORE via\nWRITE_NEXTREGS).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Values from $3F4E"},
        "6077": {"comment":"Register numbers from $0E76"},
        "6080": {"synopsis":"Writes a list of NextRegs, skipping $8F.\nEntry: DE = the register numbers (0-ended), HL = their values, one each.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"NextReg select port"},
        "6083": {"synopsis":"One register.","comment":"Next register; 0 ends"},
        "6087": {"comment":"Select it"},
        "6090": {"comment":"Memory mapping mode ($8F)?"},
        "6092": {"comment":"A = its value"},
        "6096": {"comment":"Write it, unless $8F"},
        "6098": {"synopsis":"Next register."},
        "6101": {"synopsis":"The NextRegs the Multiface sets for itself at $0195 (WRITE_NEXTREGS): 37 register numbers\nending with $00, then their 37 values at NR_INIT_VALUES. Pairs: $C0=$08 $C4=$83 $C5=$00\n$C6=$00 $14=$E3 $15=$10 $22/$26/$27/$42=$00 $43=$4E, MMU 0-7 ($50-$57) = $FF $FF $0A $0B $04\n$05 $00 $01, $68=$00 $6B=$00 $81-$85=$00 $FF $FF $FF $FF, $8C=$00, $1C=$04, $1A (clip\nwindow) = $00 $FF $00 $BF, $B8-$BB=$82 $01 $00 $F2, $0A=$11."},
        "6139": {"synopsis":"The 37 values for NR_INIT_REGS. Its 6 bytes from $17FD (MMU 0-5) are also copied to the page\ntable at $3F6A by $0202."},
        "6176": {"synopsis":"Reads a palette into memory, 2 bytes an entry (NextReg $41 the 8-bit colour, $44 the 9th\nbit).\nEntry: A = the palette control (NextReg $43) value, D = the number of entries from 0, HL =\nthe buffer.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"NextReg select port"},
        "6179": {"comment":"Palette to read"},
        "6182": {"comment":"From entry 0"},
        "6184": {"synopsis":"One entry."},
        "6185": {"comment":"Select the entry"},
        "6188": {"comment":"Its 8-bit colour ($41)"},
        "6198": {"comment":"Its 9th bit ($44)"},
        "6208": {"comment":"Next entry"},
        "6213": {"synopsis":"Writes a palette from memory through NextReg $44.\nEntry: A = the palette control (NextReg $43) value, D = the number of entries from 0, HL =\nthe colours, carry set for 2 bytes an entry (9-bit) or clear for 1.\nChanges: AF, E, D, HL.","comment":"From entry 0"},
        "6215": {"comment":"Palette to write"},
        "6218": {"synopsis":"One entry."},
        "6219": {"comment":"Select the entry"},
        "6222": {"comment":"Its first byte"},
        "6227": {"comment":"1 byte an entry?"},
        "6229": {"comment":"Its second byte (the 9th bit)"},
        "6234": {"synopsis":"Next entry.","comment":"Next entry"},
        "6239": {"synopsis":"The Multiface's RAM image: $025A bytes copied to $5B00-$5D59 by $0371 and $03D7, so each\nroutine here runs at $5B00 + (its address - $1856), with the Multiface paged out when\nneeded. It holds the paging helpers, the 128K paging copies and the 48K system variables\nfrom $5C00 (at $1956). Routine at $5B00: flips the ROM bit of both paging ports (7FFD bit 4,\n1FFD bit 2, copies at $5B5C and $5B67), turning ROM 0 into 3 and 1 into 2 and back;\ninterrupts off while writing.\nChanges: nothing."},
        "6241": {"comment":"128K paging port"},
        "6244": {"comment":"Flip the ROM bit in the copy at $5B5C"},
        "6255": {"synopsis":"Runs at $5B10: flips only the +3 ROM bit (1FFD bit 2), then pops BC and AF and returns.\nEntry: AF and BC stacked.","comment":"+3 paging port"},
        "6258": {"comment":"Flip the ROM bit in the copy at $5B67"},
        "6272": {"synopsis":"Runs at $5B21: flips the ROMs ($5B00) and jumps to the address at $5B5A. No caller in this\nROM.","comment":"Flip the ROMs"},
        "6275": {"comment":"Then jump to the address at $5B5A"},
        "6281": {"synopsis":"Runs at $5B2A: flips the +3 ROM bit ($5B10) and jumps to the address at $5B5A (through\n$5B34). No caller in this ROM.","comment":"Return to $5B34, which jumps on"},
        "6286": {"comment":"Flip the +3 ROM bit only"},
        "6291": {"synopsis":"Runs at $5B34: jumps to the address at $5B5A, HL kept."},
        "6292": {"comment":"Jump to the address at $5B5A"},
        "6297": {"synopsis":"Runs at $5B3A: pages in ROM 1 and goes to its $0AB0. No caller in this ROM.","comment":"Return to ROM 1's $0AB0"},
        "6301": {"synopsis":"Runs at $5B3E: pages in ROM 1 (NextReg $8E). The RST $18 path returns through it into the\ncalled ROM address."},
        "6306": {"synopsis":"Runs at $5B43: pages in ROM 2 (NextReg $8E); the RST $20 path."},
        "6311": {"synopsis":"Runs at $5B48: pages in ROM 3 (NextReg $8E); the RST $28 path."},
        "6316": {"synopsis":"Runs at $5B4D: pages ROM 0 back in (NextReg $8E) after a call into another ROM."},
        "6321": {"synopsis":"$5B52-$5B5B: variables. $5B54 keeps BC across the RST $10-$28 calls; $5B5A is the jump\naddress for $5B21/$5B2A/$5B34. Followed by $5B5C, the copy of port $7FFD ($07)."},
        "6332": {"synopsis":"Runs at $5B5D: ROM 3's error restart with the error code at $5B5E, stored there by $1569,\nwhich calls this through RST $28.","comment":"ROM 3's error restart"},
        "6335": {"synopsis":"$5B60-$5B72: variables. $5B67 is the copy of port $1FFD ($00); $5B6A holds the stack pointer\nkept across $13FF (initially $5BFF)."},
        "6354": {"synopsis":"Runs at $5B73: the restart byte is patched by MAP_FILL_ROM to RST $10/$18/$20/$28, which\ncalls RAM_LDIR ($5B84) with that ROM paged in.","comment":"Patched: RST $10/$18/$20/$28"},
        "6358": {"synopsis":"$5B77-$5B83: variables, all 0."},
        "6371": {"synopsis":"Runs at $5B84: LDIR, for RAM_ROM_LDIR."},
        "6374": {"synopsis":"$5B87-$5B89: variables."},
        "6377": {"synopsis":"Runs at $5B8A, called at $0284: checks the NextZXOS version and moves the program's memory\nthat the Multiface will use.\n1. Pages the Multiface out, sets port $1FFD to 0 and port $7FFD to 7 (ROM 0, bank 7 at\n   $C000).\n2. If ROM 0's word at $0006 is not $0208, pages the Multiface in and returns with carry\n   clear.\n3. Pages page $10 in at $A000 and copies four 8K blocks to DivMMC RAM: $4000-$5FFF (page\n   $0A) to bank 6, page $10 to bank 11, $C000-$DFFF (page $0E) to bank 4, $E000-$FFFF (page\n   $0F) to bank 5.\n4. Goes on to RAM_SNAP_SETUP ($5CCE), which returns with carry set.","comment":"Page the Multiface out"},
        "6380": {"comment":"Port $1FFD = 0"},
        "6386": {"comment":"Bank 7, ROM 0"},
        "6393": {"comment":"ROM 0's word at $0006"},
        "6396": {"comment":"$0208, the version expected?"},
        "6404": {"comment":"No: page the Multiface in, carry clear"},
        "6408": {"synopsis":"Version matches: copies the four 8K blocks into DivMMC banks 6, 11, 4 and 5.","comment":"Page $10 at $A000"},
        "6412": {"comment":"DivMMC bank 6 at $2000"},
        "6416": {"comment":"Copy $4000-$5FFF there"},
        "6427": {"comment":"DivMMC bank 11"},
        "6431": {"comment":"Copy page $10 there"},
        "6440": {"comment":"DivMMC bank 4"},
        "6444": {"comment":"Copy $C000-$DFFF there"},
        "6453": {"comment":"DivMMC bank 5"},
        "6457": {"comment":"Copy $E000-$FFFF there"},
        "6462": {"comment":"On to RAM_SNAP_SETUP"},
        "6465": {"synopsis":"$5BE2-$5C1B: 0s up to $5BFF (the stack at $5BFF down), then from $1956 the 48K system\nvariables' starting values: KSTATE $FF.., REPDEL $23, REPPER $02, then STRMS from $5C10 (its\nentries from $5C1C are overwritten by RAM_MF_OUT and RAM_MF_IN)."},
        "6495": {"synopsis":"$5C00: the 48K system variables start here (KSTATE)."},
        "6523": {"synopsis":"Runs at $5C1C: pages the Multiface out (a read of port $BF) with interrupts off for the read\nand on afterwards. The RST $10-$28 calls start the called ROM through it.\nChanges: nothing."},
        "6525": {"comment":"Page the Multiface out"},
        "6530": {"synopsis":"Runs at $5C23: pages the Multiface in (a read of port $3F), interrupts on afterwards. The\nRST $10-$28 calls return through it.\nChanges: nothing."},
        "6532": {"comment":"Page the Multiface in"},
        "6537": {"synopsis":"$5C2A-$5C9F: the rest of STRMS and the 48K system variables from $5C36: CHARS $3C00, RASP\n$40, PIP $00, ERR_NR $FF, ..., VARS $5CCB, CHANS $5CB6 and the other pointers to the BASIC\narea."},
        "6655": {"synopsis":"Runs at $5CA0: LDIR with a DivMMC RAM bank paged in at $2000-$3FFF and the Multiface out.\nEntry: A = the port $E3 value (CONMEM + bank), HL, DE, BC as for LDIR.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Page the Multiface out"},
        "6658": {"comment":"DivMMC bank A at $2000"},
        "6662": {"comment":"DivMMC RAM out"},
        "6665": {"comment":"Page the Multiface back in"},
        "6668": {"synopsis":"$5CAD-$5CCD: the last system variables (RAMTOP $FF57, P_RAMT $FFFF from $5CB2), the channel\ntable at $5CB6 (K, S, R, and P at $5B00), its $80 end, and the BASIC area markers."},
        "6701": {"synopsis":"Runs at $5CCE, the end of RAM_SNAP_START: prepares NextZXOS for the Multiface.\n1. Clears $C000-$FFFF (bank 7) and sets the word at $D73D to $0020.\n2. From DivMMC bank 7 copies byte $2252 to $5C81 and keeps byte $2253, clearing it.\n3. Pages the Multiface in; gets the default drive (DOS_SET_DRIVE) and its path (IDE_PATH,\n   rc_path_get, buffer at $D827); sets up the window channels (ROM 0's $2329, B = 1).\n4. Puts page 5 back at $A000; copies the path to $3A54 and the drive to $3A52, and $013C\n   bytes from $34DE of DivMMC bank 12 to $3916 (through $5E00).\n5. If the kept byte $2253 was not 0, clears $3F2E, $3E98 and the 20 breakpoint records at\n   $3EA1.\nExit: carry set, interrupts on.","comment":"Clear $C000-$FFFF"},
        "6713": {"comment":"$0020 to the word at $D73D"},
        "6719": {"comment":"DivMMC bank 7"},
        "6723": {"comment":"Its byte $2252 to $5C81"},
        "6730": {"comment":"Keep its byte $2253, then clear it"},
        "6735": {"comment":"DivMMC RAM out"},
        "6738": {"comment":"Page the Multiface in"},
        "6740": {"comment":"$FF: get the default drive"},
        "6742": {"comment":"DOS_SET_DRIVE"},
        "6745": {"comment":"Keep the drive"},
        "6759": {"comment":"rc_path_get"},
        "6761": {"comment":"IDE_PATH: the drive's path to $D827"},
        "6764": {"comment":"B = 1"},
        "6766": {"comment":"Set up the window channels"},
        "6769": {"comment":"Page 5 back at $A000"},
        "6774": {"comment":"The path, 256 bytes, to $3A54"},
        "6783": {"comment":"The drive to $3A52"},
        "6787": {"comment":"Page the Multiface out"},
        "6789": {"comment":"DivMMC bank 12"},
        "6793": {"comment":"Copy its $34DE-$3619 to $5E00"},
        "6806": {"comment":"Page the Multiface in"},
        "6810": {"comment":"Then to $3916 in Multiface RAM"},
        "6815": {"comment":"Byte $2253 was 0?"},
        "6819": {"comment":"No: clear $3F2E and $3E98"},
        "6826": {"comment":"And the 20 breakpoint records"},
        "6838": {"synopsis":"Interrupts on, carry set."},
        "6841": {"synopsis":"5 bytes copied to $D5B9 at $028A ($D5BB is then set from $3F50 at $02CB)."},
        "6846": {"synopsis":"IDE_BROWSER filetype list for saving snapshots, after expansion by $11EC (which adds the $FF\nend): length 4, \"Z80:\"."},
        "6851": {"synopsis":"IDE_BROWSER filetype list for saving bank dumps: length 4, \"BIN:\"."},
        "6856": {"synopsis":"\".z80\" and $FF: the extension $1179 puts on a snapshot's name when it lacks it (it is passed\n$1AC2, the last letter)."},
        "6861": {"synopsis":"The 4 texts that the bytes $C0-$C3 stand for when $11EC expands a text: the n-th text after\nthis $80 for byte $BF + n. $C0 INVERSE 0, $C1 INVERSE 1, $C2 space and INVERSE 0, $C3\nINVERSE 1 and space: they highlight the letter of a menu key. The texts from here on end\nwith bit 7 set, the bytes $C0-$DF excepted."},
        "6862": {"synopsis":"INVERSE 0 ($C0); also printed alone."},
        "6864": {"synopsis":"INVERSE 1 ($C1); also printed alone."},
        "6872": {"synopsis":"Help text for the snapshot file browser (2 lines)."},
        "6965": {"synopsis":"Help text for the bank dump file browser (2 lines)."},
        "7058": {"synopsis":"\"Saving...\" and a new line."},
        "7068": {"synopsis":"Plain text printed by length from $12FF: \"Version mismatch:\" (17), then from $1BA4 \"0208\nenNextMf.rom\" (17); the found version follows."},
        "7102": {"synopsis":"Shown when a snapshot is refused ($06C9)."},
        "7153": {"synopsis":"Plain text printed by length: \"Error loading enMf\" (18, from $133F), \" enMf\" (5, from $1332)\nand \".sys\" (4, from $134D) around the file's digit."},
        "7166": {"synopsis":"\" enMf\", 5 characters."},
        "7171": {"synopsis":"\".sys\", 4 characters."},
        "7175": {"synopsis":"Prompt for the snapshot's file name; texts from here end with bit 7 set, $C0-$DF excepted."},
        "7193": {"synopsis":"Prompt for the bank dump's file name."},
        "7213": {"synopsis":"INVERSE 1, \">\", INVERSE 0, printed at $1425."},
        "7217": {"synopsis":"8 bytes ending with bit 7 set ($1E $05 $0E $1A $00 $16 $17 $00): no reader found."},
        "7225": {"synopsis":"The memory view's help line and its menu (AT 22,0 first)."},
        "7365": {"synopsis":"\"Bank\" as a highlighted field."},
        "7372": {"synopsis":"\"Offset\" as a highlighted field."},
        "7382": {"synopsis":"\"Address\" as a highlighted field."},
        "7391": {"synopsis":"A space."},
        "7392": {"synopsis":"AT 0,32 and \"Enter \"; the prompts below follow it."},
        "7401": {"synopsis":"\"bank: \": the bank prompt, passed to $0B0F at $08B0."},
        "7407": {"synopsis":"\"offset: \": the offset prompt, passed to $0B16 at $08C5."},
        "7415": {"synopsis":"\"address: \": the address prompt, passed to $0B16 at $08D3."},
        "7424": {"synopsis":"\"1st offset: \": the first prompt of a range by offset, passed to $0B49 from $09BE."},
        "7436": {"synopsis":"\"1st address: \": the first prompt of a range by address, passed to $0B49 from $09C4."},
        "7449": {"synopsis":"\" last: \": the range's end prompt, passed to $0B4C at $09CB."},
        "7456": {"synopsis":"\" dest: \": the destination prompt, passed to $0B4C at $09D2."},
        "7463": {"synopsis":"\" Sure?\": the confirmation, printed through $108A at $09D9."},
        "7469": {"synopsis":"AT 0,32 and \"H/T? \"."},
        "7477": {"synopsis":"OVER 1, INVERSE 1 and a space, OVER 0, INVERSE 0, then cursor left: marks the edit position."},
        "7484": {"synopsis":"The register view's fixed text: register names placed with AT row,column (columns $42 and\n$4C: 'B' and 'L')."},
        "7682": {"synopsis":"The register view's help line and menu, then \"OS 2.08\" at AT 23,75 and \"Core \" at AT 22,73."},
        "7810": {"synopsis":"\"-->\"."},
        "7813": {"synopsis":"\"1st bank: \": the bank dump's first-bank prompt, passed to $0B0F at $077A."},
        "7823": {"synopsis":"\"last bank: \": the bank dump's last-bank prompt, passed to $0B0F at $0785."},
        "7834": {"synopsis":"The breakpoint view's help line and menu, ending with \"Global\" highlighted at AT 0,64."},
        "8002": {"synopsis":"\"c:/nextzxos/enMf0.sys\": the file $12C7 loads; the digit at $5F10 (offset 16) is replaced by\nthe file's number."},
        "8023": {"synopsis":"The message for a program that touched the +3 FDC ports (printed at $034C): FLASH 1 \"ERROR\"\nFLASH 0, then the choices reset, I and D."},
        "8149": {"synopsis":"Unused: $00 to the end of the ROM."}
      }
    }
  },
